{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NafFLcx7aUVzHQ89r3M7sW","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Full GSM8K Evaluation (N=1319)\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"N=1319全集评估baseline + RASP_20 + Standard_20，替换N=100快速评估，产出publication-quality CI。\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"baseline_gsm8k_1319\": 0.832,\n7\t      \"baseline_ci95\": [\n8\t        0.811,\n9\t        0.852\n10\t      ],\n11\t      \"rasp_20_gsm8k_1319\": 0.31,\n12\t      \"rasp_20_ci95\": [\n13\t        0.286,\n14\t        0.335\n15\t      ],\n16\t      \"standard_20_gsm8k_1319\": 0.27,\n17\t      \"standard_20_ci95\": [\n18\t        0.246,\n19\t        0.295\n20\t      ],\n21\t      \"rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp\": 4,\n22\t      \"mcnemar_p\": 0.0038,\n23\t      \"rasp_retention_rate\": 0.373,\n24\t      \"standard_retention_rate\": 0.324\n25\t    },\n26\t    \"tables\": [\n27\t      {\n28\t        \"name\": \"Post-Prune GSM8K (N=1319)\",\n29\t        \"columns\": [\n30\t          \"Method\",\n31\t          \"Sparsity\",\n32\t          \"Acc (%)\",\n33\t          \"95% CI\",\n34\t          \"Retention (%)\"\n35\t        ],\n36\t        \"rows\": [\n37\t          [\n38\t            \"Baseline\",\n39\t            \"0%\",\n40\t            83.2,\n41\t            \"[81.1, 85.2]\",\n42\t            \"—\"\n43\t          ],\n44\t          [\n45\t            \"RASP\",\n46\t            \"20%\",\n47\t            31.0,\n48\t            \"[28.6, 33.5]\",\n49\t            37.3\n50\t          ],\n51\t          [\n52\t            \"Standard\",\n53\t            \"20%\",\n54\t            27.0,\n55\t            \"[24.6, 29.5]\",\n56\t            32.4\n57\t          ]\n58\t        ]\n59\t      }\n60\t    ],\n61\t    \"figures\": [],\n62\t    \"analysis\": \"N=1319确认post-prune gap为4pp且显著。这是Recovery Amplification叙事的起点： 小的post-prune差异经过GRPO放大后变成不可逆的recovery gap。\\n\\n\\nFull N=1319确认reeval_postprune_definitive：RASP 31%、Standard 27%，gap仅4pp。 CI从±9pp（N=100）收窄到±2.5pp，McNemar在N=1319下显著（p=0.004）。Baseline 83.2%符合DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B的已知GSM8K population accuracy。4pp的 post-prune差异表明两种方法保留了相似总量的推理能力，但结构组成不同：RASP保留 功能独特的MLP groups（低F(h)锚点），Standard保留高importance的MLP groups（往 往高F(h)、高重叠）。这种组成差异在post-prune层面效果有限（4pp），但在GRPO recovery阶段被非线性放大——因为GRPO的redistribution机制对结构多样性的依赖 远强于SFT的imitation learning。\\n\"\n63\t  },\n64\t  {\n65\t    \"name\": \"SFT Warmup Recovery\",\n66\t    \"description\": \"RASP_20和Standard_20的SFT warmup恢复。[DONE — 使用实际结果]\",\n67\t    \"results\": {\n68\t      \"rasp_20_post_sft\": 0.57,\n69\t      \"standard_20_post_sft\": 0.64,\n70\t      \"rasp_sft_gain_pp\": 26,\n71\t      \"standard_sft_gain_pp\": 37,\n72\t      \"rasp_eos_rate\": 0.99,\n73\t      \"standard_eos_rate\": 0.99,\n74\t      \"rasp_train_loss_final\": 0.64,\n75\t      \"standard_train_loss_final\": 0.64\n76\t    },\n77\t    \"tables\": [\n78\t      {\n79\t        \"name\": \"Post-SFT Warmup\",\n80\t        \"columns\": [\n81\t          \"Method\",\n82\t          \"Post-Prune (%)\",\n83\t          \"Post-SFT (%)\",\n84\t          \"SFT Gain (pp)\",\n85\t          \"EOS Rate\"\n86\t        ],\n87\t        \"rows\": [\n88\t          [\n89\t            \"RASP_20\",\n90\t            31,\n91\t            57,\n92\t            26,\n93\t            0.99\n94\t          ],\n95\t          [\n96\t            \"Standard_20\",\n97\t            27,\n98\t            64,\n99\t            37,\n100\t            0.99\n101\t          ]\n102\t        ]\n103\t      }\n104\t    ],\n105\t    \"figures\": [],\n106\t    \"analysis\": \"SFT结果锚定了ranking reversal的\\\"before\\\"状态：SFT下Standard优于RASP。 GRPO（plan_003）需要将此反转。\\n\\n\\n[实际结果] Standard SFT(64%) > RASP SFT(57%)，差7pp。SFT通过模仿学习 \\\"扩展\\\"正确路径（\\\"SFT Expands\\\"），偏好高重叠结构——这正是Standard保留的结构 类型。Standard的高重叠MLP groups参与多条推理路径，提供了丰富的solution templates供SFT模仿利用。RASP保留的功能独特结构虽然对GRPO redistribution更 有利，但在SFT的imitation paradigm下利用效率较低。两者train loss均收敛到0.64、 EOS rate 99%，说明SFT学习充分、差异来自结构组成而非训练不充分。Standard SFT 优势在N=100下CI重叠（ER-001），不作为Claim 3独立证据，但与GRPO联合构成交互效应。\\n\"\n107\t  },\n108\t  {\n109\t    \"name\": \"GRPO Recovery on SFT-Warmed Models\",\n110\t    \"description\": \"GRPO Stage 2恢复。RASP和Standard均从SFT-warmed模型开始，相同超参数和计算预算。核心MVP实验。\",\n111\t    \"results\": {\n112\t      \"rasp_post_grpo_gsm8k\": 0.7,\n113\t      \"rasp_post_grpo_ci95\": [\n114\t        0.675,\n115\t        0.724\n116\t      ],\n117\t      \"standard_post_grpo_gsm8k\": 0.53,\n118\t      \"standard_post_grpo_ci95\": [\n119\t        0.503,\n120\t        0.557\n121\t      ],\n122\t      \"grpo_recovery_gap_pp\": 17,\n123\t      \"rasp_grpo_gain_over_sft_pp\": 13,\n124\t      \"standard_grpo_gain_over_sft_pp\": -11,\n125\t      \"rasp_recovery_rate\": 0.841,\n126\t      \"standard_recovery_rate\": 0.637,\n127\t      \"rasp_reward_mean_final\": 0.62,\n128\t      \"standard_reward_mean_final\": 0.45,\n129\t      \"rasp_kl_final\": 4.1,\n130\t      \"standard_kl_final\": 1.8,\n131\t      \"amplification_factor\": 4.25\n132\t    },\n133\t    \"tables\": [\n134\t      {\n135\t        \"name\": \"SFT→GRPO Recovery Pipeline\",\n136\t        \"columns\": [\n137\t          \"Method\",\n138\t          \"Post-Prune (%)\",\n139\t          \"Post-SFT (%)\",\n140\t          \"Post-GRPO (%)\",\n141\t          \"GRPO Δ (pp)\",\n142\t          \"Recovery (%)\"\n143\t        ],\n144\t        \"rows\": [\n145\t          [\n146\t            \"RASP_20\",\n147\t            31,\n148\t            57,\n149\t            70,\n150\t            13,\n151\t            84.1\n152\t          ],\n153\t          [\n154\t            \"Standard_20\",\n155\t            27,\n156\t            64,\n157\t            53,\n158\t            -11,\n159\t            63.7\n160\t          ],\n161\t          [\n162\t            \"Baseline\",\n163\t            83.2,\n164\t            \"—\",\n165\t            \"—\",\n166\t            \"—\",\n167\t            \"—\"\n168\t          ]\n169\t        ]\n170\t      }\n171\t    ],\n172\t    \"figures\": [],\n173\t    \"analysis\": \"Headline result。Ranking reversal完成：SFT下Standard>RASP (64>57)，GRPO后 RASP>>Standard (70>>53)。Standard的-11pp GRPO drop是最引人注目的发现—— GRPO不仅未帮助Standard，反而主动伤害它。Recovery Amplification confirmed。\\n\\n\\nGRPO是Recovery Amplification的核心。RASP 57%→70%（+13pp）：RASP保留的功能 独特MLP groups充当GRPO exploration的锚点，编码不可替代的推理子步骤。GRPO通过 \\\"RL Squeezes\\\"将被剪掉的高重叠groups的功能重新分配到这些锚点。reward从~0.3 稳步上升到0.62，KL=4.1表示显著policy移动——模型在积极探索并找到压缩后的推理路径。 Standard 64%→53%（-11pp）：GRPO反而伤害了Standard。Standard的高重叠结构为 SFT提供了丰富模仿模板（故SFT达64%），但缺乏功能多样性——GRPO exploration在 同质化结构空间中找不到有奖励的新路径。KL penalty逐步侵蚀SFT学到的脆弱表面 模式，exploration无法补偿损失。reward在0.45震荡（能部分答对但无法持续提升）。 核心数字：4pp post-prune gap → 17pp post-GRPO gap，amplification 4.25x。 这证明GRPO是非线性过程，对结构组成的依赖远强于SFT。\\n\"\n174\t  },\n175\t  {\n176\t    \"name\": \"Full GSM8K Eval on Recovered Models (N=1319)\",\n177\t    \"description\": \"N=1319 bootstrap CI评估所有recovered模型，产出Table 1最终数据。\",\n178\t    \"results\": {\n179\t      \"rasp_recovered_1319\": 0.7,\n180\t      \"rasp_ci95_bootstrap\": [\n181\t        0.674,\n182\t        0.724\n183\t      ],\n184\t      \"standard_recovered_1319\": 0.53,\n185\t      \"standard_ci95_bootstrap\": [\n186\t        0.503,\n187\t        0.557\n188\t      ],\n189\t      \"gap_pp\": 17,\n190\t      \"cohens_h\": 0.35,\n191\t      \"bootstrap_iterations\": 10000\n192\t    },\n193\t    \"tables\": [\n194\t      {\n195\t        \"name\": \"Table 1: Main Results at 20% Structured Sparsity\",\n196\t        \"columns\": [\n197\t          \"Method\",\n198\t          \"Post-Prune (%)\",\n199\t          \"Post-SFT (%)\",\n200\t          \"Post-SFT+GRPO (%)\",\n201\t          \"Recovery (%)\",\n202\t          \"95% CI\"\n203\t        ],\n204\t        \"rows\": [\n205\t          [\n206\t            \"Baseline\",\n207\t            83.2,\n208\t            \"—\",\n209\t            \"—\",\n210\t            \"—\",\n211\t            \"[81.1, 85.2]\"\n212\t          ],\n213\t          [\n214\t            \"RASP\",\n215\t            31,\n216\t            57,\n217\t            70,\n218\t            84.1,\n219\t            \"[67.4, 72.4]\"\n220\t          ],\n221\t          [\n222\t            \"Standard\",\n223\t            27,\n224\t            64,\n225\t            53,\n226\t            63.7,\n227\t            \"[50.3, 55.7]\"\n228\t          ],\n229\t          [\n230\t            \"GRASPrune†\",\n231\t            10,\n232\t            35,\n233\t            38,\n234\t            45.7,\n235\t            \"—\"\n236\t          ]\n237\t        ]\n238\t      }\n239\t    ],\n240\t    \"figures\": [],\n241\t    \"analysis\": \"Table 1锚定全文。同sparsity、同recovery budget，唯一区别是pruning criterion—— RASP的CKA-awareness将recovery rate从64%提升到84%（+20pp）。\\n\\n\\nBootstrap CI确认17pp gap统计稳健，CI不重叠。Cohen's h=0.35为中等偏大效应量—— 不是原始framing的\\\"巨大\\\"效应，但17pp在compressed model上是实质性差异（从 Standard的勉强可用到RASP的接近baseline性能）。这些数据填入Table 1 \\\"+SFT+GRPO\\\"列。\\n\"\n242\t  },\n243\t  {\n244\t    \"name\": \"GRASPrune Baseline at 20% Sparsity\",\n245\t    \"description\": \"GRASPrune（ACL 2026 SOTA budgeted pruning）完整pipeline。排除recovery-只-反映-post-prune-accuracy的混淆。\",\n246\t    \"results\": {\n247\t      \"grasp_post_prune_gsm8k\": 0.1,\n248\t      \"grasp_post_prune_ci95\": [\n249\t        0.084,\n250\t        0.118\n251\t      ],\n252\t      \"grasp_post_sft_gsm8k\": 0.35,\n253\t      \"grasp_post_grpo_gsm8k\": 0.38,\n254\t      \"grasp_post_grpo_ci95\": [\n255\t        0.354,\n256\t        0.407\n257\t      ],\n258\t      \"grasp_recovery_rate\": 0.457,\n259\t      \"grasp_grpo_gain_pp\": 3,\n260\t      \"grasp_vs_rasp_recovered_gap_pp\": -32\n261\t    },\n262\t    \"tables\": [\n263\t      {\n264\t        \"name\": \"GRASPrune Pipeline\",\n265\t        \"columns\": [\n266\t          \"Method\",\n267\t          \"Post-Prune (%)\",\n268\t          \"Post-SFT (%)\",\n269\t          \"Post-GRPO (%)\",\n270\t          \"GRPO Gain (pp)\"\n271\t        ],\n272\t        \"rows\": [\n273\t          [\n274\t            \"RASP\",\n275\t            31,\n276\t            57,\n277\t            70,\n278\t            13\n279\t          ],\n280\t          [\n281\t            \"Standard\",\n282\t            27,\n283\t            64,\n284\t            53,\n285\t            -11\n286\t          ],\n287\t          [\n288\t            \"GRASPrune\",\n289\t            10,\n290\t            35,\n291\t            38,\n292\t            3\n293\t          ]\n294\t        ]\n295\t      }\n296\t    ],\n297\t    \"figures\": [],\n298\t    \"analysis\": \"GRASPrune排除两个混淆：(1) RASP优势≠更好的importance estimation（GRASPrune has learned gates yet worse）；(2) recovery≠post-prune accuracy的简单函数。 CKA是recovery-optimal pruning的missing ingredient。\\n\\n\\nGRASPrune post-prune仅10%（与预实验8%/50样本一致），远低于Standard 27%。这出 人意料：GRASPrune的learned gates理论上应优于static Taylor。原因：gates通过 reconstruction loss训练，优化\\\"对语言建模最重要的结构\\\"而非\\\"对推理链最重要的 结构\\\"——perplexity-optimal和reasoning-optimal存在系统偏差。 关键发现在recovery pattern：GRASPrune 10%→38%（+28pp GRPO gain），Standard 27%→53%（+26pp）。GRASPrune起点远低于Standard（-17pp），但GRPO增量略高 （+28>+26）。这打破了\\\"recovery只是post-prune accuracy函数\\\"的线性假设：如果 recovery仅反映post-prune accuracy，GRASPrune应该恢复更少。GRASPrune gates 通过梯度流隐式保留了部分功能冗余结构，给GRPO一定redistribution空间，尽管 immediate accuracy很差。RASP（+39pp gain，31→70%）远超两者——显式CKA优化 比隐式捕获有效得多。\\n\"\n299\t  },\n300\t  {\n301\t    \"name\": \"Multi-Seed Post-Prune Evaluation (5 Seeds)\",\n302\t    \"description\": \"5种子（42,123,7,256,1337）RASP和Standard 20%剪枝+N=1319评估。Post-prune gap的统计稳健性验证。\",\n303\t    \"results\": {\n304\t      \"rasp_seeds\": {\n305\t        \"42\": 0.31,\n306\t        \"123\": 0.302,\n307\t        \"7\": 0.321,\n308\t        \"256\": 0.298,\n309\t        \"1337\": 0.324\n310\t      },\n311\t      \"rasp_mean\": 0.311,\n312\t      \"rasp_std\": 0.011,\n313\t      \"standard_seeds\": {\n314\t        \"42\": 0.27,\n315\t        \"123\": 0.258,\n316\t        \"7\": 0.275,\n317\t        \"256\": 0.261,\n318\t        \"1337\": 0.266\n319\t      },\n320\t      \"standard_mean\": 0.266,\n321\t      \"standard_std\": 0.007,\n322\t      \"paired_diffs\": [\n323\t        0.04,\n324\t        0.044,\n325\t        0.046,\n326\t        0.037,\n327\t        0.058\n328\t      ],\n329\t      \"mean_gap_pp\": 4.5,\n330\t      \"gap_std_pp\": 0.8,\n331\t      \"paired_t_p\": 0.0002,\n332\t      \"pruned_set_overlap_range\": [\n333\t        0.87,\n334\t        0.93\n335\t      ]\n336\t    },\n337\t    \"tables\": [\n338\t      {\n339\t        \"name\": \"5-Seed Robustness\",\n340\t        \"columns\": [\n341\t          \"Seed\",\n342\t          \"RASP (%)\",\n343\t          \"Standard (%)\",\n344\t          \"Gap (pp)\",\n345\t          \"Pruned Set Overlap (%)\"\n346\t        ],\n347\t        \"rows\": [\n348\t          [\n349\t            42,\n350\t            31.0,\n351\t            27.0,\n352\t            4.0,\n353\t            \"—\"\n354\t          ],\n355\t          [\n356\t            123,\n357\t            30.2,\n358\t            25.8,\n359\t            4.4,\n360\t            93\n361\t          ],\n362\t          [\n363\t            7,\n364\t            32.1,\n365\t            27.5,\n366\t            4.6,\n367\t            89\n368\t          ],\n369\t          [\n370\t            256,\n371\t            29.8,\n372\t            26.1,\n373\t            3.7,\n374\t            91\n375\t          ],\n376\t          [\n377\t            1337,\n378\t            32.4,\n379\t            26.6,\n380\t            5.8,\n381\t            87\n382\t          ],\n383\t          [\n384\t            \"Mean±Std\",\n385\t            \"31.1±1.1\",\n386\t            \"26.6±0.7\",\n387\t            \"4.5±0.8\",\n388\t            \"—\"\n389\t          ]\n390\t        ]\n391\t      }\n392\t    ],\n393\t    \"figures\": [],\n394\t    \"analysis\": \"Post-prune gap虽小（4.5pp），但5-seed p=0.0002稳健。Claim 1的post-prune component有充分统计支持。\\n\\n\\n5-seed paired t-test p=0.0002确认4.5pp gap是系统性差异。RASP σ=1.1pp， Standard σ=0.7pp——CKA和Taylor importance在512 calibration样本上已充分收敛。 所有5个seed的差异均为正（3.7-5.8pp），无reversal。Pruned set overlap 87-93% 表明~180/200 MLP groups跨seed一致，仅14-26个边界groups随calibration变化。 稳定性来源：linear CKA是kernel-based statistic，512个mean-pooled activations 提供>400有效数据点，远超stable estimation threshold。这排除了\\\"lucky seed\\\"和 \\\"calibration artifact\\\"。\\n\"\n395\t  },\n396\t  {\n397\t    \"name\": \"Scoring Ablation at 20% Sparsity\",\n398\t    \"description\": \"RASP评分函数控制消融：magnitude-only, gradient-only, random, CKA-only。隔离各组件贡献。\",\n399\t    \"results\": {\n400\t      \"rasp_full_gsm8k\": 0.31,\n401\t      \"cka_only_gsm8k\": 0.29,\n402\t      \"gradient_only_gsm8k\": 0.27,\n403\t      \"magnitude_only_gsm8k\": 0.25,\n404\t      \"random_gsm8k\": 0.18\n405\t    },\n406\t    \"tables\": [\n407\t      {\n408\t        \"name\": \"Scoring Ablation (Post-Prune)\",\n409\t        \"columns\": [\n410\t          \"Scoring\",\n411\t          \"Formula\",\n412\t          \"GSM8K (%)\",\n413\t          \"95% CI\"\n414\t        ],\n415\t        \"rows\": [\n416\t          [\n417\t            \"RASP (full)\",\n418\t            \"I(h)×(1-F(h))^α\",\n419\t            31.0,\n420\t            \"[28.6, 33.5]\"\n421\t          ],\n422\t          [\n423\t            \"CKA-only\",\n424\t            \"(1-F(h))^α\",\n425\t            29.0,\n426\t            \"[26.6, 31.5]\"\n427\t          ],\n428\t          [\n429\t            \"Gradient-only (=Std)\",\n430\t            \"I(h)\",\n431\t            27.0,\n432\t            \"[24.6, 29.5]\"\n433\t          ],\n434\t          [\n435\t            \"Magnitude-only\",\n436\t            \"||w_h||₂\",\n437\t            25.0,\n438\t            \"[22.6, 27.5]\"\n439\t          ],\n440\t          [\n441\t            \"Random\",\n442\t            \"Uniform\",\n443\t            18.0,\n444\t            \"[15.9, 20.3]\"\n445\t          ]\n446\t        ]\n447\t      }\n448\t    ],\n449\t    \"figures\": [],\n450\t    \"analysis\": \"Post-prune ablation提供组件归因。差异较小但结构清晰。需与recovery数据联合 解读——真正的区分在GRPO阶段。\\n\\n\\nPost-prune差异较小但系统性：RASP(31%)>CKA-only(29%)>gradient(27%,=Standard)> magnitude(25%)>random(18%)。CKA-only vs gradient仅差2pp，CI部分重叠——在 post-prune层面CKA的边际贡献有限。但这恰恰是Recovery Amplification要点： post-prune差异小，GRPO放大差异。Importance贡献（gradient 27% vs random 18%= 9pp）在post-prune层面实际上大于CKA边际贡献（CKA-only 29% vs gradient 27%=2pp）。 但这个关系在recovery后反转：CKA-aware结构的GRPO recoverability远高于 importance-only结构。Random at 18%确认structured scoring确实优于随机。\\n\"\n451\t  },\n452\t  {\n453\t    \"name\": \"Per-Structure CKA-Recoverability Correlation\",\n454\t    \"description\": \"MLP channel group级mixed-effects回归。N=784 MLP groups，layer random effect。控制weight norm/gradient/activation。\",\n455\t    \"results\": {\n456\t      \"n_mlp_groups\": 784,\n457\t      \"n_pruned\": 200,\n458\t      \"n_layers\": 28,\n459\t      \"cka_beta\": 0.38,\n460\t      \"cka_se\": 0.055,\n461\t      \"cka_t\": 6.91,\n462\t      \"cka_p\": 0.00034,\n463\t      \"cka_partial_r2\": 0.22,\n464\t      \"gradient_beta\": 0.12,\n465\t      \"gradient_p\": 0.019,\n466\t      \"weight_norm_beta\": 0.07,\n467\t      \"weight_norm_p\": 0.15,\n468\t      \"activation_beta\": 0.04,\n469\t      \"activation_p\": 0.42,\n470\t      \"marginal_r2\": 0.31,\n471\t      \"conditional_r2\": 0.49,\n472\t      \"icc_layer\": 0.18,\n473\t      \"vif_max\": 2.6\n474\t    },\n475\t    \"tables\": [\n476\t      {\n477\t        \"name\": \"Mixed-Effects Regression\",\n478\t        \"columns\": [\n479\t          \"Predictor\",\n480\t          \"β (std)\",\n481\t          \"SE\",\n482\t          \"p\",\n483\t          \"Partial R²\"\n484\t        ],\n485\t        \"rows\": [\n486\t          [\n487\t            \"F(h) CKA overlap\",\n488\t            0.38,\n489\t            0.055,\n490\t            \"<0.001\",\n491\t            0.22\n492\t          ],\n493\t          [\n494\t            \"I(h) gradient\",\n495\t            0.12,\n496\t            0.052,\n497\t            0.019,\n498\t            0.04\n499\t          ],\n500\t          [\n501\t            \"Weight norm\",\n502\t            0.07,\n503\t            0.05,\n504\t            0.15,\n505\t            0.01\n506\t          ],\n507\t          [\n508\t            \"Activation mag.\",\n509\t            0.04,\n510\t            0.05,\n511\t            0.42,\n512\t            \"<0.01\"\n513\t          ],\n514\t          [\n515\t            \"Marginal R²\",\n516\t            0.31,\n517\t            \"\",\n518\t            \"\",\n519\t            \"\"\n520\t          ],\n521\t          [\n522\t            \"Conditional R²\",\n523\t            0.49,\n524\t            \"\",\n525\t            \"\",\n526\t            \"\"\n527\t          ],\n528\t          [\n529\t            \"ICC (layer)\",\n530\t            0.18,\n531\t            \"\",\n532\t            \"\",\n533\t            \"\"\n534\t          ]\n535\t        ]\n536\t      }\n537\t    ],\n538\t    \"figures\": [],\n539\t    \"analysis\": \"Claim 2核心证据。CKA(β=0.38)是next-best predictor(gradient β=0.12)的3.2倍， 独立解释22%方差。验证了RASP设计理论基础。\\n\\n\\nCKA β=0.38 (p=0.0003)在控制weight norm(n.s.)、gradient(marginal p=0.019)、 activation(n.s.)后仍显著dominant，partial R²=0.22独立解释22%方差。这是因为 CKA overlap直接度量functional redundancy——\\\"这个MLP group的计算被同层其他 groups复制的程度\\\"——本质上就是\\\"GRPO能否将被剪group的功能重新分配给剩余groups\\\" 的代理指标。Weight/gradient/activation度量\\\"当前有多重要\\\"，不度量\\\"功能能否 被接管\\\"。ICC=0.18表明层间存在中等聚类：middle layers(8-18)的CKA-recoverability 耦合最强（推理redistribution集中于此），与\\\"RL Squeezes\\\"机制一致。 注意：分析仅在MLP groups(N=784)上进行，20%稀疏度下0/112 attention GQA groups 被剪——CKA信号的实际效果是在MLP groups间做reranking。\\n\"\n540\t  },\n541\t  {\n542\t    \"name\": \"SFT-Only Recovery Comparison\",\n543\t    \"description\": \"相同pruned模型、相同总计算预算，仅SFT恢复。与plan_003联合构成2×2交互分析，验证Claim 3。\",\n544\t    \"results\": {\n545\t      \"sft_only_rasp\": 0.58,\n546\t      \"sft_only_standard\": 0.66,\n547\t      \"sft_grpo_rasp\": 0.7,\n548\t      \"sft_grpo_standard\": 0.53,\n549\t      \"grpo_marginal_rasp_pp\": 12,\n550\t      \"grpo_marginal_standard_pp\": -13,\n551\t      \"interaction_pp\": 25,\n552\t      \"interaction_p\": 0.0008,\n553\t      \"rasp_adv_under_sft_pp\": -8,\n554\t      \"rasp_adv_under_grpo_pp\": 17\n555\t    },\n556\t    \"tables\": [\n557\t      {\n558\t        \"name\": \"Pruning × Recovery Interaction (2×2)\",\n559\t        \"columns\": [\n560\t          \"Pruning\",\n561\t          \"SFT-Only (%)\",\n562\t          \"SFT+GRPO (%)\",\n563\t          \"GRPO Marginal (pp)\"\n564\t        ],\n565\t        \"rows\": [\n566\t          [\n567\t            \"RASP\",\n568\t            58,\n569\t            70,\n570\t            12\n571\t          ],\n572\t          [\n573\t            \"Standard\",\n574\t            66,\n575\t            53,\n576\t            -13\n577\t          ],\n578\t          [\n579\t            \"RASP Advantage\",\n580\t            -8,\n581\t            17,\n582\t            \"—\"\n583\t          ]\n584\t        ]\n585\t      },\n586\t      {\n587\t        \"name\": \"Interaction ANOVA\",\n588\t        \"columns\": [\n589\t          \"Effect\",\n590\t          \"Estimate (pp)\",\n591\t          \"SE\",\n592\t          \"p\"\n593\t        ],\n594\t        \"rows\": [\n595\t          [\n596\t            \"Pruning (RASP-Std)\",\n597\t            4.5,\n598\t            2.8,\n599\t            \"0.11\"\n600\t          ],\n601\t          [\n602\t            \"Method (GRPO-SFT)\",\n603\t            -0.5,\n604\t            2.7,\n605\t            \"0.85\"\n606\t          ],\n607\t          [\n608\t            \"Pruning × Method\",\n609\t            25,\n610\t            3.8,\n611\t            \"0.0008\"\n612\t          ]\n613\t        ]\n614\t      }\n615\t    ],\n616\t    \"figures\": [],\n617\t    \"analysis\": \"交互p=0.0008直接支持Claim 3。Main effects不显著而interaction显著——optimal pruning取决于recovery method。这是novel finding。\\n\\n\\nExtended SFT（全预算）RASP=58%、Standard=66%，与warmup SFT接近（SFT饱和快）。 核心交互： SFT-only: Standard(66%) > RASP(58%) → Standard wins by 8pp SFT+GRPO: RASP(70%) > Standard(53%) → RASP wins by 17pp → 完整ranking reversal。交互效应=12-(-13)=25pp, p=0.0008。 机制：\\\"SFT Expands\\\"偏好高重叠结构（Standard保留的），模仿学习在多条重叠路径 上同时强化。\\\"RL Squeezes\\\"需要功能独特锚点（RASP保留的），exploration要求 结构多样性来发现新推理路径。Standard缺乏这些锚点，GRPO的KL penalty在无 rewarding exploration下侵蚀SFT patterns。 最引人入胜的发现：pruning主效应不显著（p≈0.11）——RASP和Standard\\\"平均\\\"差不多。 Method主效应也不显著（p≈0.85）——SFT和GRPO\\\"平均\\\"差不多。但交互25pp, p<0.001 ——pruning选择和recovery方法间存在质变性交互。\\n\"\n618\t  },\n619\t  {\n620\t    \"name\": \"25% Sparsity RASP + Standard\",\n621\t    \"description\": \"25%稀疏度完整pipeline，测试RASP优势在更高压缩下的表现和sparsity scaling。\",\n622\t    \"results\": {\n623\t      \"rasp_25_post_prune\": 0.2,\n624\t      \"standard_25_post_prune\": 0.12,\n625\t      \"rasp_25_gap_pp\": 8,\n626\t      \"rasp_25_post_sft\": 0.42,\n627\t      \"standard_25_post_sft\": 0.36,\n628\t      \"rasp_25_post_grpo\": 0.55,\n629\t      \"standard_25_post_grpo\": 0.32,\n630\t      \"rasp_25_recovery_gap_pp\": 23,\n631\t      \"rasp_25_recovery_rate\": 0.661,\n632\t      \"standard_25_recovery_rate\": 0.385\n633\t    },\n634\t    \"tables\": [\n635\t      {\n636\t        \"name\": \"Multi-Sparsity Comparison\",\n637\t        \"columns\": [\n638\t          \"Sparsity\",\n639\t          \"Method\",\n640\t          \"Post-Prune (%)\",\n641\t          \"Post-GRPO (%)\",\n642\t          \"Recovery (%)\",\n643\t          \"Gap (pp)\"\n644\t        ],\n645\t        \"rows\": [\n646\t          [\n647\t            \"20%\",\n648\t            \"RASP\",\n649\t            31,\n650\t            70,\n651\t            84.1,\n652\t            \"\"\n653\t          ],\n654\t          [\n655\t            \"20%\",\n656\t            \"Standard\",\n657\t            27,\n658\t            53,\n659\t            63.7,\n660\t            17\n661\t          ],\n662\t          [\n663\t            \"25%\",\n664\t            \"RASP\",\n665\t            20,\n666\t            55,\n667\t            66.1,\n668\t            \"\"\n669\t          ],\n670\t          [\n671\t            \"25%\",\n672\t            \"Standard\",\n673\t            12,\n674\t            32,\n675\t            38.5,\n676\t            23\n677\t          ]\n678\t        ]\n679\t      }\n680\t    ],\n681\t    \"figures\": [],\n682\t    \"analysis\": \"25%确认RASP优势不是单一操作点artifact。Recovery gap从17→23pp说明CKA-awareness 在更高压缩下价值更大。\\n\\n\\n25%稀疏度放大了post-prune gap（8pp vs 20%的4pp）：额外5%移除不成比例影响 Standard——importance-based策略在高稀疏度下被迫移除更多functionally unique groups（它们的importance低），而RASP仍优先保护这些groups。 Recovery gap也扩大：23pp(55% vs 32%)，vs 20%的17pp。但amplification factor 下降（23/8=2.88x vs 20%的4.25x），因为RASP在25%也开始受损——更多unique groups被迫移除，GRPO redistribution空间缩小。 RASP graceful degradation（84→66% recovery rate）vs Standard accelerating collapse（64→39%）支持RASP在多稀疏度下的实用价值。\\n\"\n683\t  },\n684\t  {\n685\t    \"name\": \"30% Sparsity Probe\",\n686\t    \"description\": \"30%稀疏度prune+eval only，映射collapse threshold和RASP的操作包络。\",\n687\t    \"results\": {\n688\t      \"rasp_30_post_prune\": 0.08,\n689\t      \"rasp_30_ci95\": [\n690\t        0.065,\n691\t        0.098\n692\t      ],\n693\t      \"standard_30_post_prune\": 0.03,\n694\t      \"standard_30_ci95\": [\n695\t        0.02,\n696\t        0.044\n697\t      ]\n698\t    },\n699\t    \"tables\": [\n700\t      {\n701\t        \"name\": \"Sparsity Collapse Map\",\n702\t        \"columns\": [\n703\t          \"Sparsity\",\n704\t          \"Method\",\n705\t          \"Post-Prune (%)\",\n706\t          \"Status\"\n707\t        ],\n708\t        \"rows\": [\n709\t          [\n710\t            \"20%\",\n711\t            \"RASP\",\n712\t            31,\n713\t            \"Recoverable\"\n714\t          ],\n715\t          [\n716\t            \"20%\",\n717\t            \"Standard\",\n718\t            27,\n719\t            \"Partial\"\n720\t          ],\n721\t          [\n722\t            \"25%\",\n723\t            \"RASP\",\n724\t            20,\n725\t            \"Recoverable\"\n726\t          ],\n727\t          [\n728\t            \"25%\",\n729\t            \"Standard\",\n730\t            12,\n731\t            \"Weak\"\n732\t          ],\n733\t          [\n734\t            \"30%\",\n735\t            \"RASP\",\n736\t            8,\n737\t            \"Near-collapse\"\n738\t          ],\n739\t          [\n740\t            \"30%\",\n741\t            \"Standard\",\n742\t            3,\n743\t            \"Collapsed\"\n744\t          ],\n745\t          [\n746\t            \"35%\",\n747\t            \"Both\",\n748\t            0,\n749\t            \"Collapsed (D005)\"\n750\t          ]\n751\t        ]\n752\t      }\n753\t    ],\n754\t    \"figures\": [],\n755\t    \"analysis\": \"完成RASP操作包络映射。Appendix/Discussion材料，回应\\\"为什么选20%\\\"。\\n\\n\\n30% RASP降至8%，Standard降至3%。RASP仍非零但已入collapse zone，与D005 35% 完全collapse一致。DeepSeek-R1-Distill模型的\\\"可恢复稀疏度\\\"上界：~25%有效 操作范围，30%边界，35%+崩溃。不进行recovery：8% post-prune的reward signal 极稀疏，GRPO难以收敛。Distilled模型的冗余预算天然小于natively-trained模型， 因为distillation已经压缩了表示。\\n\"\n756\t  },\n757\t  {\n758\t    \"name\": \"OOD Evaluation (MATH-500, HumanEval)\",\n759\t    \"description\": \"Recovered models在GSM8K之外benchmark评估，验证RASP优势的OOD泛化。\",\n760\t    \"results\": {\n761\t      \"baseline_math500\": 0.7,\n762\t      \"rasp_recovered_math500\": 0.55,\n763\t      \"standard_recovered_math500\": 0.42,\n764\t      \"rasp_math500_advantage_pp\": 13,\n765\t      \"baseline_humaneval\": 0.5,\n766\t      \"rasp_recovered_humaneval\": 0.4,\n767\t      \"standard_recovered_humaneval\": 0.33,\n768\t      \"rasp_humaneval_advantage_pp\": 7,\n769\t      \"rasp_mean_ood_retention\": 0.793,\n770\t      \"standard_mean_ood_retention\": 0.63\n771\t    },\n772\t    \"tables\": [\n773\t      {\n774\t        \"name\": \"Cross-Benchmark OOD Evaluation\",\n775\t        \"columns\": [\n776\t          \"Benchmark\",\n777\t          \"Baseline (%)\",\n778\t          \"RASP (%)\",\n779\t          \"Standard (%)\",\n780\t          \"RASP Adv. (pp)\"\n781\t        ],\n782\t        \"rows\": [\n783\t          [\n784\t            \"GSM8K\",\n785\t            83.2,\n786\t            70,\n787\t            53,\n788\t            17\n789\t          ],\n790\t          [\n791\t            \"MATH-500\",\n792\t            70,\n793\t            55,\n794\t            42,\n795\t            13\n796\t          ],\n797\t          [\n798\t            \"HumanEval\",\n799\t            50,\n800\t            40,\n801\t            33,\n802\t            7\n803\t          ]\n804\t        ]\n805\t      }\n806\t    ],\n807\t    \"figures\": [],\n808\t    \"analysis\": \"OOD泛化将paper从GSM8K-specific提升为general reasoning compression method。 7-17pp一致优势回应reviewer的generalization concern。\\n\\n\\nMATH-500上RASP优势13pp（55% vs 42%），HumanEval上7pp（40% vs 33%）。 MATH-500优势更大因为MATH需要更深推理链（多步数学推导），RASP保留的functionally unique结构在深层推理中价值更高。HumanEval更依赖pattern matching/syntax knowledge，pruning影响相对较小。RASP retention: GSM8K 84%, MATH-500 79%, HumanEval 80%——一致~80%+ retention说明RASP保留的是通用推理scaffold而非 GSM8K-specific patterns。Standard retention: GSM8K 64%, MATH-500 60%, HumanEval 66%——也一致但低~20pp。\\n\"\n809\t  },\n810\t  {\n811\t    \"name\": \"Bonsai Baseline at 20% Sparsity\",\n812\t    \"description\": \"Bonsai（ICML 2025）gradient-free结构化剪枝。补充external baseline。\",\n813\t    \"results\": {\n814\t      \"bonsai_post_prune\": 0.24,\n815\t      \"bonsai_post_sft\": 0.5,\n816\t      \"bonsai_post_grpo\": 0.47,\n817\t      \"bonsai_grpo_gain_pp\": -3,\n818\t      \"bonsai_recovery_rate\": 0.565\n819\t    },\n820\t    \"tables\": [\n821\t      {\n822\t        \"name\": \"Extended Baselines\",\n823\t        \"columns\": [\n824\t          \"Method\",\n825\t          \"Post-Prune (%)\",\n826\t          \"Post-GRPO (%)\",\n827\t          \"GRPO Δ (pp)\"\n828\t        ],\n829\t        \"rows\": [\n830\t          [\n831\t            \"RASP\",\n832\t            31,\n833\t            70,\n834\t            13\n835\t          ],\n836\t          [\n837\t            \"Standard\",\n838\t            27,\n839\t            53,\n840\t            -11\n841\t          ],\n842\t          [\n843\t            \"Bonsai\",\n844\t            24,\n845\t            47,\n846\t            -3\n847\t          ],\n848\t          [\n849\t            \"GRASPrune\",\n850\t            10,\n851\t            38,\n852\t            3\n853\t          ]\n854\t        ]\n855\t      }\n856\t    ],\n857\t    \"figures\": [],\n858\t    \"analysis\": \"Bonsai补全baseline方阵。GRPO benefit pattern: RASP(+13) >> GRASPrune(+3) > Bonsai(-3) > Standard(-11)。CKA-awareness是关键区分因素。\\n\\n\\nBonsai activation-based importance，post-prune 24%略低于Standard 27%（Taylor importance在此模型上稍优，gradient signal捕获了更多推理相关信息）。GRPO对 Bonsai也产生负效应（-3pp），与Standard pattern一致：importance-without-CKA 方法保留高重叠结构，缺乏GRPO所需的功能独特锚点。4种non-CKA方法中仅GRASPrune 从GRPO微弱获益（+3pp，因其gates隐式捕获了部分冗余信息），Standard(-11pp)和 Bonsai(-3pp)均受损。GRPO benefit不是普遍现象，而需要CKA-aware结构组成。\\n\"\n859\t  },\n860\t  {\n861\t    \"name\": \"CKA Reliability Analysis\",\n862\t    \"description\": \"Split-half consistency和calibration size sensitivity，CKA scoring可靠性验证。\",\n863\t    \"results\": {\n864\t      \"split_half_rho\": 0.93,\n865\t      \"split_half_p\": \"<0.0001\",\n866\t      \"cal_256_gsm8k\": 0.29,\n867\t      \"cal_512_gsm8k\": 0.31,\n868\t      \"cal_1024_gsm8k\": 0.32,\n869\t      \"cal_256_vs_512_rank_corr\": 0.9,\n870\t      \"cal_512_vs_1024_rank_corr\": 0.97,\n871\t      \"pruned_overlap_256_512\": 0.86,\n872\t      \"pruned_overlap_512_1024\": 0.95\n873\t    },\n874\t    \"tables\": [\n875\t      {\n876\t        \"name\": \"CKA Reliability\",\n877\t        \"columns\": [\n878\t          \"Analysis\",\n879\t          \"Metric\",\n880\t          \"Value\"\n881\t        ],\n882\t        \"rows\": [\n883\t          [\n884\t            \"Split-half\",\n885\t            \"Spearman ρ\",\n886\t            0.93\n887\t          ],\n888\t          [\n889\t            \"Cal 256\",\n890\t            \"GSM8K (%)\",\n891\t            29\n892\t          ],\n893\t          [\n894\t            \"Cal 512\",\n895\t            \"GSM8K (%)\",\n896\t            31\n897\t          ],\n898\t          [\n899\t            \"Cal 1024\",\n900\t            \"GSM8K (%)\",\n901\t            32\n902\t          ]\n903\t        ]\n904\t      }\n905\t    ],\n906\t    \"figures\": [],\n907\t    \"analysis\": \"Appendix材料，main text一行引用。\\n\\n\\nSplit-half ρ=0.93，linear CKA在512样本上已收敛。Calibration size影响微小： 256→512提升2pp(29→31%)，512→1024仅1pp(31→32%)，总range 3pp小于inter-seed variance。512是near-optimal calibration size。核心剪枝决策（pruned set overlap 86-95%）对calibration不敏感。Housekeeping but essential for credibility。\\n\"\n908\t  },\n909\t  {\n910\t    \"name\": \"α Sensitivity Ablation\",\n911\t    \"description\": \"α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0}，RASP唯一自由参数的系统性分析。\",\n912\t    \"results\": {\n913\t      \"alpha_0_0\": 0.25,\n914\t      \"alpha_0_25\": 0.27,\n915\t      \"alpha_0_5\": 0.29,\n916\t      \"alpha_1_0\": 0.31,\n917\t      \"alpha_2_0\": 0.35,\n918\t      \"optimal_alpha\": 2.0,\n919\t      \"optimal_vs_alpha0_gap_pp\": 10,\n920\t      \"curve_shape\": \"monotonically increasing, diminishing returns\"\n921\t    },\n922\t    \"tables\": [\n923\t      {\n924\t        \"name\": \"α Ablation\",\n925\t        \"columns\": [\n926\t          \"α\",\n927\t          \"Emphasis\",\n928\t          \"GSM8K (%)\",\n929\t          \"Δ vs α=0 (pp)\"\n930\t        ],\n931\t        \"rows\": [\n932\t          [\n933\t            0.0,\n934\t            \"Importance-only\",\n935\t            25,\n936\t            0\n937\t          ],\n938\t          [\n939\t            0.25,\n940\t            \"Weak CKA\",\n941\t            27,\n942\t            2\n943\t          ],\n944\t          [\n945\t            0.5,\n946\t            \"Moderate CKA\",\n947\t            29,\n948\t            4\n949\t          ],\n950\t          [\n951\t            1.0,\n952\t            \"Balanced (default)\",\n953\t            31,\n954\t            6\n955\t          ],\n956\t          [\n957\t            2.0,\n958\t            \"Strong CKA\",\n959\t            35,\n960\t            10\n961\t          ]\n962\t        ]\n963\t      }\n964\t    ],\n965\t    \"figures\": [],\n966\t    \"analysis\": \"Dream reviewers全档位Critical实验。10pp gap量化CKA贡献。曲线未见peak说明 optimal α可能>2.0，motivates future auto-tuning。\\n\\n\\nα=0（importance-only within RASP framework）给出25%，低于Standard 27%。原因： RASP使用reasoning-trace calibration（CoT traces）计算importance，CoT traces 较长噪声较高，产生比standard perplexity-calibration稍差的importance estimates。 CKA组件补偿并超过差距：α=0.5已达29%（超Standard 27%），α=2.0达35%。 曲线单调递增+diminishing returns：0→0.5增4pp，0.5→1.0增2pp，1.0→2.0增4pp （高α端acceleration提示optimal可能>2.0，与预实验α=4.0=40%一致）。 最优vs α=0 gap=10pp量化了CKA作为pruning signal的价值。α是唯一free parameter， 此ablation为practitioners提供调参指导：α=1合理default，α∈[1,2]推荐范围。\\n\"\n967\t  },\n968\t  {\n969\t    \"name\": \"Inference Speedup Benchmark\",\n970\t    \"description\": \"Wall-clock latency + throughput比较。结构化剪枝的practical motivation。\",\n971\t    \"results\": {\n972\t      \"dense_latency_ms\": 12.4,\n973\t      \"rasp_20_latency_ms\": 9.7,\n974\t      \"standard_20_latency_ms\": 9.6,\n975\t      \"rasp_20_speedup\": 1.28,\n976\t      \"dense_throughput_tok_s\": 80.6,\n977\t      \"rasp_20_throughput_tok_s\": 103.1,\n978\t      \"memory_reduction_pct\": 18.5,\n979\t      \"unstructured_20_speedup\": 1.02\n980\t    },\n981\t    \"tables\": [\n982\t      {\n983\t        \"name\": \"Inference Benchmark\",\n984\t        \"columns\": [\n985\t          \"Model\",\n986\t          \"Latency (ms/tok)\",\n987\t          \"Speedup\",\n988\t          \"Throughput (tok/s)\"\n989\t        ],\n990\t        \"rows\": [\n991\t          [\n992\t            \"Dense\",\n993\t            12.4,\n994\t            \"1.00x\",\n995\t            80.6\n996\t          ],\n997\t          [\n998\t            \"RASP 20%\",\n999\t            9.7,\n1000\t            \"1.28x\",\n1001\t            103.1\n1002\t          ],\n1003\t          [\n1004\t            \"Unstructured 20%\",\n1005\t            12.2,\n1006\t            \"1.02x\",\n1007\t            82.0\n1008\t          ]\n1009\t        ]\n1010\t      }\n1011\t    ],\n1012\t    \"figures\": [],\n1013\t    \"analysis\": \"1.28x加速 + 70% accuracy提供明确practical motivation。Structured RASP在 accuracy和speed两个维度均胜unstructured。\\n\\n\\n20%结构化稀疏度提供1.28x实际加速（12.4→9.7 ms/tok），因为移除200个MLP channel groups直接减少矩阵维度，不需sparse hardware。RASP和Standard speedup 几乎相同（均~1.28x），因为两者移除相同数量structures。Memory减少18.5%。 对比unstructured 20%（仅1.02x，需sparse tensor cores），structured pruning 的practical value明确。RASP在accuracy(70%) + speed(1.28x)两个维度均优于 unstructured(60%, 1.02x)。\\n\"\n1014\t  },\n1015\t  {\n1016\t    \"name\": \"Unstructured Pruning Baseline at 20%\",\n1017\t    \"description\": \"Magnitude-based unstructured 20%。标定structured vs unstructured gap，对标Self-Healing。\",\n1018\t    \"results\": {\n1019\t      \"unstructured_post_prune\": 0.45,\n1020\t      \"unstructured_post_sft\": 0.55,\n1021\t      \"unstructured_post_grpo\": 0.6,\n1022\t      \"unstructured_grpo_gain_pp\": 5,\n1023\t      \"unstructured_recovery_rate\": 0.721,\n1024\t      \"unstructured_speedup\": 1.02\n1025\t    },\n1026\t    \"tables\": [\n1027\t      {\n1028\t        \"name\": \"Structured vs Unstructured\",\n1029\t        \"columns\": [\n1030\t          \"Method\",\n1031\t          \"Post-Prune (%)\",\n1032\t          \"Post-GRPO (%)\",\n1033\t          \"Speedup\"\n1034\t        ],\n1035\t        \"rows\": [\n1036\t          [\n1037\t            \"RASP (structured)\",\n1038\t            31,\n1039\t            70,\n1040\t            \"1.28x\"\n1041\t          ],\n1042\t          [\n1043\t            \"Standard (structured)\",\n1044\t            27,\n1045\t            53,\n1046\t            \"1.29x\"\n1047\t          ],\n1048\t          [\n1049\t            \"Unstructured 20%\",\n1050\t            45,\n1051\t            60,\n1052\t            \"1.02x\"\n1053\t          ]\n1054\t        ]\n1055\t      }\n1056\t    ],\n1057\t    \"figures\": [],\n1058\t    \"analysis\": \"RASP structured在accuracy(70>60)和speed(1.28>1.02)双维度优于unstructured。 完成\\\"为什么structured pruning\\\"论证。\\n\\n\\nUnstructured 20% post-prune 45%远高于structured RASP 31%——保留了所有architectural structures，仅均匀削弱每个structure的capacity。但post-GRPO仅60%，低于RASP 70%。 看似反直觉：起点更高却恢复更低。原因：unstructured均匀削弱所有structures， GRPO的redistribution机制在此设置下效率低——没有完整结构可以\\\"接管\\\"被削弱结构 的功能。RASP的结构化移除创造了明确的donor(移除的高重叠groups)和receiver (保留的独特groups)，GRPO可清晰地将donor功能重分配给receiver。 关键比较：RASP structured(70%, 1.28x) vs unstructured(60%, 1.02x)——accuracy 和speed双维度RASP占优。对标Self-Healing(2025)的unstructured设置。\\n\"\n1059\t  },\n1060\t  {\n1061\t    \"name\": \"SFT OOD Eval Contingency\",\n1062\t    \"description\": \"SFT-recovered模型的OOD评估。检验Standard SFT 64%的GSM8K-specificity。\",\n1063\t    \"results\": {\n1064\t      \"standard_sft_math500\": 0.35,\n1065\t      \"standard_sft_humaneval\": 0.25,\n1066\t      \"rasp_sft_math500\": 0.42,\n1067\t      \"rasp_sft_humaneval\": 0.32,\n1068\t      \"standard_gsm8k_to_math500_retention\": 0.538,\n1069\t      \"rasp_gsm8k_to_math500_retention\": 0.724\n1070\t    },\n1071\t    \"tables\": [\n1072\t      {\n1073\t        \"name\": \"SFT OOD Transfer\",\n1074\t        \"columns\": [\n1075\t          \"Method\",\n1076\t          \"GSM8K (%)\",\n1077\t          \"MATH-500 (%)\",\n1078\t          \"HumanEval (%)\",\n1079\t          \"MATH Ret. (%)\"\n1080\t        ],\n1081\t        \"rows\": [\n1082\t          [\n1083\t            \"RASP SFT-only\",\n1084\t            58,\n1085\t            42,\n1086\t            32,\n1087\t            72.4\n1088\t          ],\n1089\t          [\n1090\t            \"Standard SFT-only\",\n1091\t            66,\n1092\t            35,\n1093\t            25,\n1094\t            53.8\n1095\t          ]\n1096\t        ]\n1097\t      }\n1098\t    ],\n1099\t    \"figures\": [],\n1100\t    \"analysis\": \"Standard SFT优势是shallow，RASP GRPO优势是deep。Discussion增加\\\"surface vs genuine reasoning recovery\\\"分析维度。\\n\\nBest tier下GRPO advantage=17pp远超5pp阈值（contingency不strictly needed）， 但仍提供有价值分析。Standard SFT从GSM8K 66%降至MATH-500 35%（retention 53%）， RASP SFT从58%降至42%（retention 72%）。Standard的OOD drop更剧烈：其SFT recovery包含显著GSM8K-specific pattern learning——SFT在高重叠结构上学到了 GSM8K特定的数字操作模板，不泛化到MATH。RASP的SFT recovery虽GSM8K绝对数低， 但泛化性好，因为functionally unique结构支持更通用推理。 补充Claim 3：SFT下Standard的优势是shallow(GSM8K-specific)，GRPO下RASP的 优势是deep(OOD-generalizable)。\\n\"\n1101\t  }\n1102\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b567d72f-e483-48d7-8fff-91c8c788b5c9","uuid":"296752fe-7d2d-4eb1-9218-199177a2c3c3","timestamp":"2026-05-15T14:37:20.356Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T140651/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Full GSM8K Evaluation (N=1319)\",\n    \"description\": \"N=1319全集评估baseline + RASP_20 + Standard_20，替换N=100快速评估，产出publication-quality CI。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"baseline_gsm8k_1319\": 0.832,\n      \"baseline_ci95\": [\n        0.811,\n        0.852\n      ],\n      \"rasp_20_gsm8k_1319\": 0.31,\n      \"rasp_20_ci95\": [\n        0.286,\n        0.335\n      ],\n      \"standard_20_gsm8k_1319\": 0.27,\n      \"standard_20_ci95\": [\n        0.246,\n        0.295\n      ],\n      \"rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp\": 4,\n      \"mcnemar_p\": 0.0038,\n      \"rasp_retention_rate\": 0.373,\n      \"standard_retention_rate\": 0.324\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Post-Prune GSM8K (N=1319)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Sparsity\",\n          \"Acc (%)\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"Retention (%)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Baseline\",\n            \"0%\",\n            83.2,\n            \"[81.1, 85.2]\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RASP\",\n            \"20%\",\n            31.0,\n            \"[28.6, 33.5]\",\n            37.3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard\",\n            \"20%\",\n            27.0,\n            \"[24.6, 29.5]\",\n            32.4\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"N=1319确认post-prune gap为4pp且显著。这是Recovery Amplification叙事的起点： 小的post-prune差异经过GRPO放大后变成不可逆的recovery gap。\\n\\n\\nFull N=1319确认reeval_postprune_definitive：RASP 31%、Standard 27%，gap仅4pp。 CI从±9pp（N=100）收窄到±2.5pp，McNemar在N=1319下显著（p=0.004）。Baseline 83.2%符合DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B的已知GSM8K population accuracy。4pp的 post-prune差异表明两种方法保留了相似总量的推理能力，但结构组成不同：RASP保留 功能独特的MLP groups（低F(h)锚点），Standard保留高importance的MLP groups（往 往高F(h)、高重叠）。这种组成差异在post-prune层面效果有限（4pp），但在GRPO recovery阶段被非线性放大——因为GRPO的redistribution机制对结构多样性的依赖 远强于SFT的imitation learning。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SFT Warmup Recovery\",\n    \"description\": \"RASP_20和Standard_20的SFT warmup恢复。[DONE — 使用实际结果]\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_20_post_sft\": 0.57,\n      \"standard_20_post_sft\": 0.64,\n      \"rasp_sft_gain_pp\": 26,\n      \"standard_sft_gain_pp\": 37,\n      \"rasp_eos_rate\": 0.99,\n      \"standard_eos_rate\": 0.99,\n      \"rasp_train_loss_final\": 0.64,\n      \"standard_train_loss_final\": 0.64\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Post-SFT Warmup\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Post-Prune (%)\",\n          \"Post-SFT (%)\",\n          \"SFT Gain (pp)\",\n          \"EOS Rate\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP_20\",\n            31,\n            57,\n            26,\n            0.99\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard_20\",\n            27,\n            64,\n            37,\n            0.99\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"SFT结果锚定了ranking reversal的\\\"before\\\"状态：SFT下Standard优于RASP。 GRPO（plan_003）需要将此反转。\\n\\n\\n[实际结果] Standard SFT(64%) > RASP SFT(57%)，差7pp。SFT通过模仿学习 \\\"扩展\\\"正确路径（\\\"SFT Expands\\\"），偏好高重叠结构——这正是Standard保留的结构 类型。Standard的高重叠MLP groups参与多条推理路径，提供了丰富的solution templates供SFT模仿利用。RASP保留的功能独特结构虽然对GRPO redistribution更 有利，但在SFT的imitation paradigm下利用效率较低。两者train loss均收敛到0.64、 EOS rate 99%，说明SFT学习充分、差异来自结构组成而非训练不充分。Standard SFT 优势在N=100下CI重叠（ER-001），不作为Claim 3独立证据，但与GRPO联合构成交互效应。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"GRPO Recovery on SFT-Warmed Models\",\n    \"description\": \"GRPO Stage 2恢复。RASP和Standard均从SFT-warmed模型开始，相同超参数和计算预算。核心MVP实验。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_post_grpo_gsm8k\": 0.7,\n      \"rasp_post_grpo_ci95\": [\n        0.675,\n        0.724\n      ],\n      \"standard_post_grpo_gsm8k\": 0.53,\n      \"standard_post_grpo_ci95\": [\n        0.503,\n        0.557\n      ],\n      \"grpo_recovery_gap_pp\": 17,\n      \"rasp_grpo_gain_over_sft_pp\": 13,\n      \"standard_grpo_gain_over_sft_pp\": -11,\n      \"rasp_recovery_rate\": 0.841,\n      \"standard_recovery_rate\": 0.637,\n      \"rasp_reward_mean_final\": 0.62,\n      \"standard_reward_mean_final\": 0.45,\n      \"rasp_kl_final\": 4.1,\n      \"standard_kl_final\": 1.8,\n      \"amplification_factor\": 4.25\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"SFT→GRPO Recovery Pipeline\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Post-Prune (%)\",\n          \"Post-SFT (%)\",\n          \"Post-GRPO (%)\",\n          \"GRPO Δ (pp)\",\n          \"Recovery (%)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP_20\",\n            31,\n            57,\n            70,\n            13,\n            84.1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard_20\",\n            27,\n            64,\n            53,\n            -11,\n            63.7\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Baseline\",\n            83.2,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Headline result。Ranking reversal完成：SFT下Standard>RASP (64>57)，GRPO后 RASP>>Standard (70>>53)。Standard的-11pp GRPO drop是最引人注目的发现—— GRPO不仅未帮助Standard，反而主动伤害它。Recovery Amplification confirmed。\\n\\n\\nGRPO是Recovery Amplification的核心。RASP 57%→70%（+13pp）：RASP保留的功能 独特MLP groups充当GRPO exploration的锚点，编码不可替代的推理子步骤。GRPO通过 \\\"RL Squeezes\\\"将被剪掉的高重叠groups的功能重新分配到这些锚点。reward从~0.3 稳步上升到0.62，KL=4.1表示显著policy移动——模型在积极探索并找到压缩后的推理路径。 Standard 64%→53%（-11pp）：GRPO反而伤害了Standard。Standard的高重叠结构为 SFT提供了丰富模仿模板（故SFT达64%），但缺乏功能多样性——GRPO exploration在 同质化结构空间中找不到有奖励的新路径。KL penalty逐步侵蚀SFT学到的脆弱表面 模式，exploration无法补偿损失。reward在0.45震荡（能部分答对但无法持续提升）。 核心数字：4pp post-prune gap → 17pp post-GRPO gap，amplification 4.25x。 这证明GRPO是非线性过程，对结构组成的依赖远强于SFT。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Full GSM8K Eval on Recovered Models (N=1319)\",\n    \"description\": \"N=1319 bootstrap CI评估所有recovered模型，产出Table 1最终数据。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_recovered_1319\": 0.7,\n      \"rasp_ci95_bootstrap\": [\n        0.674,\n        0.724\n      ],\n      \"standard_recovered_1319\": 0.53,\n      \"standard_ci95_bootstrap\": [\n        0.503,\n        0.557\n      ],\n      \"gap_pp\": 17,\n      \"cohens_h\": 0.35,\n      \"bootstrap_iterations\": 10000\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 1: Main Results at 20% Structured Sparsity\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Post-Prune (%)\",\n          \"Post-SFT (%)\",\n          \"Post-SFT+GRPO (%)\",\n          \"Recovery (%)\",\n          \"95% CI\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Baseline\",\n            83.2,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"[81.1, 85.2]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RASP\",\n            31,\n            57,\n            70,\n            84.1,\n            \"[67.4, 72.4]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard\",\n            27,\n            64,\n            53,\n            63.7,\n            \"[50.3, 55.7]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GRASPrune†\",\n            10,\n            35,\n            38,\n            45.7,\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Table 1锚定全文。同sparsity、同recovery budget，唯一区别是pruning criterion—— RASP的CKA-awareness将recovery rate从64%提升到84%（+20pp）。\\n\\n\\nBootstrap CI确认17pp gap统计稳健，CI不重叠。Cohen's h=0.35为中等偏大效应量—— 不是原始framing的\\\"巨大\\\"效应，但17pp在compressed model上是实质性差异（从 Standard的勉强可用到RASP的接近baseline性能）。这些数据填入Table 1 \\\"+SFT+GRPO\\\"列。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"GRASPrune Baseline at 20% Sparsity\",\n    \"description\": \"GRASPrune（ACL 2026 SOTA budgeted pruning）完整pipeline。排除recovery-只-反映-post-prune-accuracy的混淆。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"grasp_post_prune_gsm8k\": 0.1,\n      \"grasp_post_prune_ci95\": [\n        0.084,\n        0.118\n      ],\n      \"grasp_post_sft_gsm8k\": 0.35,\n      \"grasp_post_grpo_gsm8k\": 0.38,\n      \"grasp_post_grpo_ci95\": [\n        0.354,\n        0.407\n      ],\n      \"grasp_recovery_rate\": 0.457,\n      \"grasp_grpo_gain_pp\": 3,\n      \"grasp_vs_rasp_recovered_gap_pp\": -32\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"GRASPrune Pipeline\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Post-Prune (%)\",\n          \"Post-SFT (%)\",\n          \"Post-GRPO (%)\",\n          \"GRPO Gain (pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP\",\n            31,\n            57,\n            70,\n            13\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard\",\n            27,\n            64,\n            53,\n            -11\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GRASPrune\",\n            10,\n            35,\n            38,\n            3\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"GRASPrune排除两个混淆：(1) RASP优势≠更好的importance estimation（GRASPrune has learned gates yet worse）；(2) recovery≠post-prune accuracy的简单函数。 CKA是recovery-optimal pruning的missing ingredient。\\n\\n\\nGRASPrune post-prune仅10%（与预实验8%/50样本一致），远低于Standard 27%。这出 人意料：GRASPrune的learned gates理论上应优于static Taylor。原因：gates通过 reconstruction loss训练，优化\\\"对语言建模最重要的结构\\\"而非\\\"对推理链最重要的 结构\\\"——perplexity-optimal和reasoning-optimal存在系统偏差。 关键发现在recovery pattern：GRASPrune 10%→38%（+28pp GRPO gain），Standard 27%→53%（+26pp）。GRASPrune起点远低于Standard（-17pp），但GRPO增量略高 （+28>+26）。这打破了\\\"recovery只是post-prune accuracy函数\\\"的线性假设：如果 recovery仅反映post-prune accuracy，GRASPrune应该恢复更少。GRASPrune gates 通过梯度流隐式保留了部分功能冗余结构，给GRPO一定redistribution空间，尽管 immediate accuracy很差。RASP（+39pp gain，31→70%）远超两者——显式CKA优化 比隐式捕获有效得多。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-Seed Post-Prune Evaluation (5 Seeds)\",\n    \"description\": \"5种子（42,123,7,256,1337）RASP和Standard 20%剪枝+N=1319评估。Post-prune gap的统计稳健性验证。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_seeds\": {\n        \"42\": 0.31,\n        \"123\": 0.302,\n        \"7\": 0.321,\n        \"256\": 0.298,\n        \"1337\": 0.324\n      },\n      \"rasp_mean\": 0.311,\n      \"rasp_std\": 0.011,\n      \"standard_seeds\": {\n        \"42\": 0.27,\n        \"123\": 0.258,\n        \"7\": 0.275,\n        \"256\": 0.261,\n        \"1337\": 0.266\n      },\n      \"standard_mean\": 0.266,\n      \"standard_std\": 0.007,\n      \"paired_diffs\": [\n        0.04,\n        0.044,\n        0.046,\n        0.037,\n        0.058\n      ],\n      \"mean_gap_pp\": 4.5,\n      \"gap_std_pp\": 0.8,\n      \"paired_t_p\": 0.0002,\n      \"pruned_set_overlap_range\": [\n        0.87,\n        0.93\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"5-Seed Robustness\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Seed\",\n          \"RASP (%)\",\n          \"Standard (%)\",\n          \"Gap (pp)\",\n          \"Pruned Set Overlap (%)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            42,\n            31.0,\n            27.0,\n            4.0,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            123,\n            30.2,\n            25.8,\n            4.4,\n            93\n          ],\n          [\n            7,\n            32.1,\n            27.5,\n            4.6,\n            89\n          ],\n          [\n            256,\n            29.8,\n            26.1,\n            3.7,\n            91\n          ],\n          [\n            1337,\n            32.4,\n            26.6,\n            5.8,\n            87\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mean±Std\",\n            \"31.1±1.1\",\n            \"26.6±0.7\",\n            \"4.5±0.8\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Post-prune gap虽小（4.5pp），但5-seed p=0.0002稳健。Claim 1的post-prune component有充分统计支持。\\n\\n\\n5-seed paired t-test p=0.0002确认4.5pp gap是系统性差异。RASP σ=1.1pp， Standard σ=0.7pp——CKA和Taylor importance在512 calibration样本上已充分收敛。 所有5个seed的差异均为正（3.7-5.8pp），无reversal。Pruned set overlap 87-93% 表明~180/200 MLP groups跨seed一致，仅14-26个边界groups随calibration变化。 稳定性来源：linear CKA是kernel-based statistic，512个mean-pooled activations 提供>400有效数据点，远超stable estimation threshold。这排除了\\\"lucky seed\\\"和 \\\"calibration artifact\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Scoring Ablation at 20% Sparsity\",\n    \"description\": \"RASP评分函数控制消融：magnitude-only, gradient-only, random, CKA-only。隔离各组件贡献。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_full_gsm8k\": 0.31,\n      \"cka_only_gsm8k\": 0.29,\n      \"gradient_only_gsm8k\": 0.27,\n      \"magnitude_only_gsm8k\": 0.25,\n      \"random_gsm8k\": 0.18\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Scoring Ablation (Post-Prune)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Scoring\",\n          \"Formula\",\n          \"GSM8K (%)\",\n          \"95% CI\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP (full)\",\n            \"I(h)×(1-F(h))^α\",\n            31.0,\n            \"[28.6, 33.5]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CKA-only\",\n            \"(1-F(h))^α\",\n            29.0,\n            \"[26.6, 31.5]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gradient-only (=Std)\",\n            \"I(h)\",\n            27.0,\n            \"[24.6, 29.5]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Magnitude-only\",\n            \"||w_h||₂\",\n            25.0,\n            \"[22.6, 27.5]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random\",\n            \"Uniform\",\n            18.0,\n            \"[15.9, 20.3]\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Post-prune ablation提供组件归因。差异较小但结构清晰。需与recovery数据联合 解读——真正的区分在GRPO阶段。\\n\\n\\nPost-prune差异较小但系统性：RASP(31%)>CKA-only(29%)>gradient(27%,=Standard)> magnitude(25%)>random(18%)。CKA-only vs gradient仅差2pp，CI部分重叠——在 post-prune层面CKA的边际贡献有限。但这恰恰是Recovery Amplification要点： post-prune差异小，GRPO放大差异。Importance贡献（gradient 27% vs random 18%= 9pp）在post-prune层面实际上大于CKA边际贡献（CKA-only 29% vs gradient 27%=2pp）。 但这个关系在recovery后反转：CKA-aware结构的GRPO recoverability远高于 importance-only结构。Random at 18%确认structured scoring确实优于随机。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Per-Structure CKA-Recoverability Correlation\",\n    \"description\": \"MLP channel group级mixed-effects回归。N=784 MLP groups，layer random effect。控制weight norm/gradient/activation。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_mlp_groups\": 784,\n      \"n_pruned\": 200,\n      \"n_layers\": 28,\n      \"cka_beta\": 0.38,\n      \"cka_se\": 0.055,\n      \"cka_t\": 6.91,\n      \"cka_p\": 0.00034,\n      \"cka_partial_r2\": 0.22,\n      \"gradient_beta\": 0.12,\n      \"gradient_p\": 0.019,\n      \"weight_norm_beta\": 0.07,\n      \"weight_norm_p\": 0.15,\n      \"activation_beta\": 0.04,\n      \"activation_p\": 0.42,\n      \"marginal_r2\": 0.31,\n      \"conditional_r2\": 0.49,\n      \"icc_layer\": 0.18,\n      \"vif_max\": 2.6\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Mixed-Effects Regression\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Predictor\",\n          \"β (std)\",\n          \"SE\",\n          \"p\",\n          \"Partial R²\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"F(h) CKA overlap\",\n            0.38,\n            0.055,\n            \"<0.001\",\n            0.22\n          ],\n          [\n            \"I(h) gradient\",\n            0.12,\n            0.052,\n            0.019,\n            0.04\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Weight norm\",\n            0.07,\n            0.05,\n            0.15,\n            0.01\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Activation mag.\",\n            0.04,\n            0.05,\n            0.42,\n            \"<0.01\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Marginal R²\",\n            0.31,\n            \"\",\n            \"\",\n            \"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Conditional R²\",\n            0.49,\n            \"\",\n            \"\",\n            \"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ICC (layer)\",\n            0.18,\n            \"\",\n            \"\",\n            \"\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Claim 2核心证据。CKA(β=0.38)是next-best predictor(gradient β=0.12)的3.2倍， 独立解释22%方差。验证了RASP设计理论基础。\\n\\n\\nCKA β=0.38 (p=0.0003)在控制weight norm(n.s.)、gradient(marginal p=0.019)、 activation(n.s.)后仍显著dominant，partial R²=0.22独立解释22%方差。这是因为 CKA overlap直接度量functional redundancy——\\\"这个MLP group的计算被同层其他 groups复制的程度\\\"——本质上就是\\\"GRPO能否将被剪group的功能重新分配给剩余groups\\\" 的代理指标。Weight/gradient/activation度量\\\"当前有多重要\\\"，不度量\\\"功能能否 被接管\\\"。ICC=0.18表明层间存在中等聚类：middle layers(8-18)的CKA-recoverability 耦合最强（推理redistribution集中于此），与\\\"RL Squeezes\\\"机制一致。 注意：分析仅在MLP groups(N=784)上进行，20%稀疏度下0/112 attention GQA groups 被剪——CKA信号的实际效果是在MLP groups间做reranking。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SFT-Only Recovery Comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"相同pruned模型、相同总计算预算，仅SFT恢复。与plan_003联合构成2×2交互分析，验证Claim 3。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sft_only_rasp\": 0.58,\n      \"sft_only_standard\": 0.66,\n      \"sft_grpo_rasp\": 0.7,\n      \"sft_grpo_standard\": 0.53,\n      \"grpo_marginal_rasp_pp\": 12,\n      \"grpo_marginal_standard_pp\": -13,\n      \"interaction_pp\": 25,\n      \"interaction_p\": 0.0008,\n      \"rasp_adv_under_sft_pp\": -8,\n      \"rasp_adv_under_grpo_pp\": 17\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Pruning × Recovery Interaction (2×2)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Pruning\",\n          \"SFT-Only (%)\",\n          \"SFT+GRPO (%)\",\n          \"GRPO Marginal (pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP\",\n            58,\n            70,\n            12\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard\",\n            66,\n            53,\n            -13\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RASP Advantage\",\n            -8,\n            17,\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Interaction ANOVA\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Effect\",\n          \"Estimate (pp)\",\n          \"SE\",\n          \"p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Pruning (RASP-Std)\",\n            4.5,\n            2.8,\n            \"0.11\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Method (GRPO-SFT)\",\n            -0.5,\n            2.7,\n            \"0.85\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Pruning × Method\",\n            25,\n            3.8,\n            \"0.0008\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"交互p=0.0008直接支持Claim 3。Main effects不显著而interaction显著——optimal pruning取决于recovery method。这是novel finding。\\n\\n\\nExtended SFT（全预算）RASP=58%、Standard=66%，与warmup SFT接近（SFT饱和快）。 核心交互： SFT-only: Standard(66%) > RASP(58%) → Standard wins by 8pp SFT+GRPO: RASP(70%) > Standard(53%) → RASP wins by 17pp → 完整ranking reversal。交互效应=12-(-13)=25pp, p=0.0008。 机制：\\\"SFT Expands\\\"偏好高重叠结构（Standard保留的），模仿学习在多条重叠路径 上同时强化。\\\"RL Squeezes\\\"需要功能独特锚点（RASP保留的），exploration要求 结构多样性来发现新推理路径。Standard缺乏这些锚点，GRPO的KL penalty在无 rewarding exploration下侵蚀SFT patterns。 最引人入胜的发现：pruning主效应不显著（p≈0.11）——RASP和Standard\\\"平均\\\"差不多。 Method主效应也不显著（p≈0.85）——SFT和GRPO\\\"平均\\\"差不多。但交互25pp, p<0.001 ——pruning选择和recovery方法间存在质变性交互。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"25% Sparsity RASP + Standard\",\n    \"description\": \"25%稀疏度完整pipeline，测试RASP优势在更高压缩下的表现和sparsity scaling。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_25_post_prune\": 0.2,\n      \"standard_25_post_prune\": 0.12,\n      \"rasp_25_gap_pp\": 8,\n      \"rasp_25_post_sft\": 0.42,\n      \"standard_25_post_sft\": 0.36,\n      \"rasp_25_post_grpo\": 0.55,\n      \"standard_25_post_grpo\": 0.32,\n      \"rasp_25_recovery_gap_pp\": 23,\n      \"rasp_25_recovery_rate\": 0.661,\n      \"standard_25_recovery_rate\": 0.385\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Multi-Sparsity Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Sparsity\",\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Post-Prune (%)\",\n          \"Post-GRPO (%)\",\n          \"Recovery (%)\",\n          \"Gap (pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"20%\",\n            \"RASP\",\n            31,\n            70,\n            84.1,\n            \"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"20%\",\n            \"Standard\",\n            27,\n            53,\n            63.7,\n            17\n          ],\n          [\n            \"25%\",\n            \"RASP\",\n            20,\n            55,\n            66.1,\n            \"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"25%\",\n            \"Standard\",\n            12,\n            32,\n            38.5,\n            23\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"25%确认RASP优势不是单一操作点artifact。Recovery gap从17→23pp说明CKA-awareness 在更高压缩下价值更大。\\n\\n\\n25%稀疏度放大了post-prune gap（8pp vs 20%的4pp）：额外5%移除不成比例影响 Standard——importance-based策略在高稀疏度下被迫移除更多functionally unique groups（它们的importance低），而RASP仍优先保护这些groups。 Recovery gap也扩大：23pp(55% vs 32%)，vs 20%的17pp。但amplification factor 下降（23/8=2.88x vs 20%的4.25x），因为RASP在25%也开始受损——更多unique groups被迫移除，GRPO redistribution空间缩小。 RASP graceful degradation（84→66% recovery rate）vs Standard accelerating collapse（64→39%）支持RASP在多稀疏度下的实用价值。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"30% Sparsity Probe\",\n    \"description\": \"30%稀疏度prune+eval only，映射collapse threshold和RASP的操作包络。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_30_post_prune\": 0.08,\n      \"rasp_30_ci95\": [\n        0.065,\n        0.098\n      ],\n      \"standard_30_post_prune\": 0.03,\n      \"standard_30_ci95\": [\n        0.02,\n        0.044\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Sparsity Collapse Map\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Sparsity\",\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Post-Prune (%)\",\n          \"Status\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"20%\",\n            \"RASP\",\n            31,\n            \"Recoverable\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"20%\",\n            \"Standard\",\n            27,\n            \"Partial\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"25%\",\n            \"RASP\",\n            20,\n            \"Recoverable\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"25%\",\n            \"Standard\",\n            12,\n            \"Weak\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"30%\",\n            \"RASP\",\n            8,\n            \"Near-collapse\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"30%\",\n            \"Standard\",\n            3,\n            \"Collapsed\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"35%\",\n            \"Both\",\n            0,\n            \"Collapsed (D005)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"完成RASP操作包络映射。Appendix/Discussion材料，回应\\\"为什么选20%\\\"。\\n\\n\\n30% RASP降至8%，Standard降至3%。RASP仍非零但已入collapse zone，与D005 35% 完全collapse一致。DeepSeek-R1-Distill模型的\\\"可恢复稀疏度\\\"上界：~25%有效 操作范围，30%边界，35%+崩溃。不进行recovery：8% post-prune的reward signal 极稀疏，GRPO难以收敛。Distilled模型的冗余预算天然小于natively-trained模型， 因为distillation已经压缩了表示。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OOD Evaluation (MATH-500, HumanEval)\",\n    \"description\": \"Recovered models在GSM8K之外benchmark评估，验证RASP优势的OOD泛化。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"baseline_math500\": 0.7,\n      \"rasp_recovered_math500\": 0.55,\n      \"standard_recovered_math500\": 0.42,\n      \"rasp_math500_advantage_pp\": 13,\n      \"baseline_humaneval\": 0.5,\n      \"rasp_recovered_humaneval\": 0.4,\n      \"standard_recovered_humaneval\": 0.33,\n      \"rasp_humaneval_advantage_pp\": 7,\n      \"rasp_mean_ood_retention\": 0.793,\n      \"standard_mean_ood_retention\": 0.63\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cross-Benchmark OOD Evaluation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Baseline (%)\",\n          \"RASP (%)\",\n          \"Standard (%)\",\n          \"RASP Adv. (pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            83.2,\n            70,\n            53,\n            17\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MATH-500\",\n            70,\n            55,\n            42,\n            13\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HumanEval\",\n            50,\n            40,\n            33,\n            7\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"OOD泛化将paper从GSM8K-specific提升为general reasoning compression method。 7-17pp一致优势回应reviewer的generalization concern。\\n\\n\\nMATH-500上RASP优势13pp（55% vs 42%），HumanEval上7pp（40% vs 33%）。 MATH-500优势更大因为MATH需要更深推理链（多步数学推导），RASP保留的functionally unique结构在深层推理中价值更高。HumanEval更依赖pattern matching/syntax knowledge，pruning影响相对较小。RASP retention: GSM8K 84%, MATH-500 79%, HumanEval 80%——一致~80%+ retention说明RASP保留的是通用推理scaffold而非 GSM8K-specific patterns。Standard retention: GSM8K 64%, MATH-500 60%, HumanEval 66%——也一致但低~20pp。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Bonsai Baseline at 20% Sparsity\",\n    \"description\": \"Bonsai（ICML 2025）gradient-free结构化剪枝。补充external baseline。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"bonsai_post_prune\": 0.24,\n      \"bonsai_post_sft\": 0.5,\n      \"bonsai_post_grpo\": 0.47,\n      \"bonsai_grpo_gain_pp\": -3,\n      \"bonsai_recovery_rate\": 0.565\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Extended Baselines\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Post-Prune (%)\",\n          \"Post-GRPO (%)\",\n          \"GRPO Δ (pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP\",\n            31,\n            70,\n            13\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard\",\n            27,\n            53,\n            -11\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Bonsai\",\n            24,\n            47,\n            -3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GRASPrune\",\n            10,\n            38,\n            3\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Bonsai补全baseline方阵。GRPO benefit pattern: RASP(+13) >> GRASPrune(+3) > Bonsai(-3) > Standard(-11)。CKA-awareness是关键区分因素。\\n\\n\\nBonsai activation-based importance，post-prune 24%略低于Standard 27%（Taylor importance在此模型上稍优，gradient signal捕获了更多推理相关信息）。GRPO对 Bonsai也产生负效应（-3pp），与Standard pattern一致：importance-without-CKA 方法保留高重叠结构，缺乏GRPO所需的功能独特锚点。4种non-CKA方法中仅GRASPrune 从GRPO微弱获益（+3pp，因其gates隐式捕获了部分冗余信息），Standard(-11pp)和 Bonsai(-3pp)均受损。GRPO benefit不是普遍现象，而需要CKA-aware结构组成。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"CKA Reliability Analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Split-half consistency和calibration size sensitivity，CKA scoring可靠性验证。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"split_half_rho\": 0.93,\n      \"split_half_p\": \"<0.0001\",\n      \"cal_256_gsm8k\": 0.29,\n      \"cal_512_gsm8k\": 0.31,\n      \"cal_1024_gsm8k\": 0.32,\n      \"cal_256_vs_512_rank_corr\": 0.9,\n      \"cal_512_vs_1024_rank_corr\": 0.97,\n      \"pruned_overlap_256_512\": 0.86,\n      \"pruned_overlap_512_1024\": 0.95\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"CKA Reliability\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Analysis\",\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Value\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Split-half\",\n            \"Spearman ρ\",\n            0.93\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Cal 256\",\n            \"GSM8K (%)\",\n            29\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Cal 512\",\n            \"GSM8K (%)\",\n            31\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Cal 1024\",\n            \"GSM8K (%)\",\n            32\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Appendix材料，main text一行引用。\\n\\n\\nSplit-half ρ=0.93，linear CKA在512样本上已收敛。Calibration size影响微小： 256→512提升2pp(29→31%)，512→1024仅1pp(31→32%)，总range 3pp小于inter-seed variance。512是near-optimal calibration size。核心剪枝决策（pruned set overlap 86-95%）对calibration不敏感。Housekeeping but essential for credibility。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"α Sensitivity Ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0}，RASP唯一自由参数的系统性分析。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"alpha_0_0\": 0.25,\n      \"alpha_0_25\": 0.27,\n      \"alpha_0_5\": 0.29,\n      \"alpha_1_0\": 0.31,\n      \"alpha_2_0\": 0.35,\n      \"optimal_alpha\": 2.0,\n      \"optimal_vs_alpha0_gap_pp\": 10,\n      \"curve_shape\": \"monotonically increasing, diminishing returns\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"α Ablation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"α\",\n          \"Emphasis\",\n          \"GSM8K (%)\",\n          \"Δ vs α=0 (pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            0.0,\n            \"Importance-only\",\n            25,\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            0.25,\n            \"Weak CKA\",\n            27,\n            2\n          ],\n          [\n            0.5,\n            \"Moderate CKA\",\n            29,\n            4\n          ],\n          [\n            1.0,\n            \"Balanced (default)\",\n            31,\n            6\n          ],\n          [\n            2.0,\n            \"Strong CKA\",\n            35,\n            10\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Dream reviewers全档位Critical实验。10pp gap量化CKA贡献。曲线未见peak说明 optimal α可能>2.0，motivates future auto-tuning。\\n\\n\\nα=0（importance-only within RASP framework）给出25%，低于Standard 27%。原因： RASP使用reasoning-trace calibration（CoT traces）计算importance，CoT traces 较长噪声较高，产生比standard perplexity-calibration稍差的importance estimates。 CKA组件补偿并超过差距：α=0.5已达29%（超Standard 27%），α=2.0达35%。 曲线单调递增+diminishing returns：0→0.5增4pp，0.5→1.0增2pp，1.0→2.0增4pp （高α端acceleration提示optimal可能>2.0，与预实验α=4.0=40%一致）。 最优vs α=0 gap=10pp量化了CKA作为pruning signal的价值。α是唯一free parameter， 此ablation为practitioners提供调参指导：α=1合理default，α∈[1,2]推荐范围。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Inference Speedup Benchmark\",\n    \"description\": \"Wall-clock latency + throughput比较。结构化剪枝的practical motivation。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dense_latency_ms\": 12.4,\n      \"rasp_20_latency_ms\": 9.7,\n      \"standard_20_latency_ms\": 9.6,\n      \"rasp_20_speedup\": 1.28,\n      \"dense_throughput_tok_s\": 80.6,\n      \"rasp_20_throughput_tok_s\": 103.1,\n      \"memory_reduction_pct\": 18.5,\n      \"unstructured_20_speedup\": 1.02\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Inference Benchmark\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"Latency (ms/tok)\",\n          \"Speedup\",\n          \"Throughput (tok/s)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Dense\",\n            12.4,\n            \"1.00x\",\n            80.6\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RASP 20%\",\n            9.7,\n            \"1.28x\",\n            103.1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Unstructured 20%\",\n            12.2,\n            \"1.02x\",\n            82.0\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"1.28x加速 + 70% accuracy提供明确practical motivation。Structured RASP在 accuracy和speed两个维度均胜unstructured。\\n\\n\\n20%结构化稀疏度提供1.28x实际加速（12.4→9.7 ms/tok），因为移除200个MLP channel groups直接减少矩阵维度，不需sparse hardware。RASP和Standard speedup 几乎相同（均~1.28x），因为两者移除相同数量structures。Memory减少18.5%。 对比unstructured 20%（仅1.02x，需sparse tensor cores），structured pruning 的practical value明确。RASP在accuracy(70%) + speed(1.28x)两个维度均优于 unstructured(60%, 1.02x)。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Unstructured Pruning Baseline at 20%\",\n    \"description\": \"Magnitude-based unstructured 20%。标定structured vs unstructured gap，对标Self-Healing。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"unstructured_post_prune\": 0.45,\n      \"unstructured_post_sft\": 0.55,\n      \"unstructured_post_grpo\": 0.6,\n      \"unstructured_grpo_gain_pp\": 5,\n      \"unstructured_recovery_rate\": 0.721,\n      \"unstructured_speedup\": 1.02\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Structured vs Unstructured\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Post-Prune (%)\",\n          \"Post-GRPO (%)\",\n          \"Speedup\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP (structured)\",\n            31,\n            70,\n            \"1.28x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard (structured)\",\n            27,\n            53,\n            \"1.29x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Unstructured 20%\",\n            45,\n            60,\n            \"1.02x\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"RASP structured在accuracy(70>60)和speed(1.28>1.02)双维度优于unstructured。 完成\\\"为什么structured pruning\\\"论证。\\n\\n\\nUnstructured 20% post-prune 45%远高于structured RASP 31%——保留了所有architectural structures，仅均匀削弱每个structure的capacity。但post-GRPO仅60%，低于RASP 70%。 看似反直觉：起点更高却恢复更低。原因：unstructured均匀削弱所有structures， GRPO的redistribution机制在此设置下效率低——没有完整结构可以\\\"接管\\\"被削弱结构 的功能。RASP的结构化移除创造了明确的donor(移除的高重叠groups)和receiver (保留的独特groups)，GRPO可清晰地将donor功能重分配给receiver。 关键比较：RASP structured(70%, 1.28x) vs unstructured(60%, 1.02x)——accuracy 和speed双维度RASP占优。对标Self-Healing(2025)的unstructured设置。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SFT OOD Eval Contingency\",\n    \"description\": \"SFT-recovered模型的OOD评估。检验Standard SFT 64%的GSM8K-specificity。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"standard_sft_math500\": 0.35,\n      \"standard_sft_humaneval\": 0.25,\n      \"rasp_sft_math500\": 0.42,\n      \"rasp_sft_humaneval\": 0.32,\n      \"standard_gsm8k_to_math500_retention\": 0.538,\n      \"rasp_gsm8k_to_math500_retention\": 0.724\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"SFT OOD Transfer\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"GSM8K (%)\",\n          \"MATH-500 (%)\",\n          \"HumanEval (%)\",\n          \"MATH Ret. (%)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP SFT-only\",\n            58,\n            42,\n            32,\n            72.4\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard SFT-only\",\n            66,\n            35,\n            25,\n            53.8\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Standard SFT优势是shallow，RASP GRPO优势是deep。Discussion增加\\\"surface vs genuine reasoning recovery\\\"分析维度。\\n\\nBest tier下GRPO advantage=17pp远超5pp阈值（contingency不strictly needed）， 但仍提供有价值分析。Standard SFT从GSM8K 66%降至MATH-500 35%（retention 53%）， RASP SFT从58%降至42%（retention 72%）。Standard的OOD drop更剧烈：其SFT recovery包含显著GSM8K-specific pattern learning——SFT在高重叠结构上学到了 GSM8K特定的数字操作模板，不泛化到MATH。RASP的SFT recovery虽GSM8K绝对数低， 但泛化性好，因为functionally unique结构支持更通用推理。 补充Claim 3：SFT下Standard的优势是shallow(GSM8K-specific)，GRPO下RASP的 优势是deep(OOD-generalizable)。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":1102,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1102}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01U2CDKJxixKVCJMHR3AmxYk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FMoUXqwZwWfaE88xtD3ZKK","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T140651/best/paper_framing.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11367,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11367},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b567d72f-e483-48d7-8fff-91c8c788b5c9","uuid":"c0b760ce-59eb-409c-9c5e-4cc9dfc42af4"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FMoUXqwZwWfaE88xtD3ZKK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — recovery_aware_struct_prune\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25 submission)\n5\t- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n6\t- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026\n7\t\n8\t## Core Insight (Redundancy Paradox)\n9\tTraditional structured pruning selects structures to remove based on importance metrics alone (weight magnitude, gradient sensitivity). We show this misses a critical signal for RLVR recovery: **functional uniqueness**. Structures with high functional overlap (high CKA) can be safely pruned because RLVR redistributes their function across retained structures. Structures with low overlap are functionally irreplaceable — once removed, even RLVR cannot recreate their unique contribution. This creates a **Redundancy Paradox**: protecting functionally unique structures matters more for recovery than protecting high-importance structures.\n10\t\n11\tRASP exploits this via S(h) = I(h) × (1-F(h))^α: high overlap → low score → **pruned first**; low overlap → high score → **protected**. The result: RASP preferentially removes functionally redundant structures (whose function RLVR can recover) while Standard pruning may accidentally remove functionally unique structures that happen to have low importance scores. At 20% sparsity, this effect manifests entirely within MLP channel groups (0/112 attention GQA groups are pruned under either method; all 200 pruned structures are MLP groups), consistent with the \"RL Squeezes, SFT Expands\" mechanism (ICLR 2026).\n12\t\n13\t## Core Claims (3)\n14\t\n15\t1. **CKA-aware pruning preserves reasoning ability**: At matched sparsity and parameter count, RASP preserves significantly more post-prune reasoning accuracy than importance-only pruning (MVP evidence: 29% vs 1% GSM8K at 20% sparsity, p<0.0001), and this gap enables qualitatively different recovery outcomes (RASP-pruned models can be recovered via RLVR; standard-pruned models cannot).\n16\t\n17\t2. **Functional overlap predicts per-structure recoverability** *(scope: MLP channel groups at moderate sparsity)*: Per-structure CKA functional overlap F(h) is a stronger predictor of post-recovery accuracy retention than standard importance metrics alone, within the MLP channel groups that are actually pruned at 20-25% sparsity. At these sparsity levels, attention GQA groups consistently rank above all MLP groups in the global importance list (0/112 pruned); the CKA signal's practical effect is selecting *which* MLP groups to prune (N=784, ~200 pruned). Validated via mixed-effects regression (layer as random effect) on MLP groups, controlling for weight norm, gradient importance, and activation magnitude. Cross-component (attention + MLP) validation requires higher sparsity (~40%+).\n18\t\n19\t3. **Recovery method conditions optimal pruning order**: The relative ranking of pruning strategies changes depending on recovery method (RLVR vs SFT). Structures expendable under RLVR recovery may be critical under SFT recovery, consistent with the \"RL Squeezes, SFT Expands\" mechanism — RLVR compresses incorrect paths (tolerates removal of overlapping structures) while SFT expands correct paths (needs preserved trajectory-encoding structures).\n20\t\n21\t## Story Spine\n22\t\n23\t- **Problem**: Structured pruning for reasoning LLMs optimizes for immediate post-pruning accuracy, treating subsequent recovery as independent. At moderate sparsity (20-35%), this disconnect can be catastrophic: standard importance-based pruning collapses reasoning ability to near-zero, making recovery impossible regardless of method. The choice of what to prune determines whether recovery can succeed at all.\n24\t\n25\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Self-Healing (2025) shows RLVR recovers pruned reasoning models to 95%+ at 25% compression but uses standard pruning and tests only one ratio. GRASPrune (ACL 2026) provides SOTA budgeted structural pruning but doesn't study reasoning-specific recovery. RESP (Dec 2025) uses reasoning-trace calibration but has no recovery phase. No work studies how the pruning structure choice interacts with RLVR recovery quality, or whether optimal pruning differs for RLVR vs SFT recovery.\n26\t\n27\t- **Our framing**: We introduce Recovery-Aware Structured Pruning (RASP), reframing structural redundancy from a flaw to eliminate into a signal of RLVR recoverability. RASP scores structures by S(h) = I(h) × (1 - F(h))^α, protecting functionally unique reasoning scaffolding while allowing removal of structures whose function can be redistributed through RLVR. This connects to the Lottery Ticket Hypothesis at a new level: LTH asks \"which subnetwork trains well\" (binary); RASP asks \"which structures to remove so the remainder recovers well under a specific training paradigm\" (paradigm-conditioned trainability).\n28\t\n29\t- **Headline result template**: \"At 20% structured sparsity on DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B, RASP preserves 29% GSM8K accuracy (vs 1% for standard pruning), enabling RLVR recovery to X% while standard-pruned models remain unrecoverable. Per-structure CKA overlap explains Y% of variance in recovery outcomes (mixed-effects β = Z, p < 0.001).\"\n30\t\n31\t## Venue Fit\n32\t- EMNLP Efficient Methods track: natural fit for structured pruning + reasoning model recovery\n33\t- Reasoning model compression is timely (DeepSeek-R1, QwQ, etc. driving demand)\n34\t- Empirical rigor + mechanistic analysis aligns with EMNLP's preference for thorough experimentation\n35\t\n36\t## Venue Fit Risks\n37\t- **\"Just another pruning metric\"**: Mitigate with Redundancy Paradox framing, LTH generalization (paradigm-conditioned trainability), and mechanistic analysis showing WHY it works\n38\t- **\"Single model\"**: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B is the most widely-used open reasoning model; multi-sparsity + multi-method comparison compensates\n39\t- **\"MPruner already uses CKA\"**: Different granularity (intra-layer per-head vs inter-layer), different objective (recoverability prediction vs redundancy removal), different domain (reasoning LLM vs CNN/general transformer)\n40\t- **\"Cross-component pruning not observed\"**: At 20-25% sparsity, only MLP groups are pruned (0 attention groups). Framework scores both types jointly, but global ranking at moderate sparsity naturally prioritizes MLP removal. Mitigate by: (1) honest description of actual pruning distribution, (2) noting the CKA signal still drives 29% vs 1% gap via MLP group reranking, (3) optionally test higher sparsity where attention groups enter pruning range\n41\t\n42\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Experimental Responses\n43\t\n44\t| Concern | Response | Supporting Experiment |\n45\t|---------|----------|----------------------|\n46\t| Incremental over importance-only pruning | 28pp post-prune gap is qualitative, not incremental; enables vs prevents recovery | exp-001, exp-002 |\n47\t| CKA overlap might correlate with simpler metrics | Scoring ablation: CKA vs magnitude/gradient/random | exp-007 |\n48\t| Single model generalization | Multi-sparsity (20%, 25%, 30%) + multi-method (Standard, GRASPrune, RASP) | exp-003, exp-005 |\n49\t| RLVR vs SFT claim needs controlled comparison | Same pruned models, same data budget, different recovery method | exp-006 |\n50\t| Statistical rigor of correlation claim | Mixed-effects regression with covariates on MLP groups (N=784, ~200 pruned) | exp-008 |\n51\t| Only MLP groups pruned at 20% sparsity | Honest description + CKA still drives 29% vs 1% via MLP reranking + optional higher sparsity test | experiments.tex |\n52\t| Recovery might just reflect post-prune accuracy | Include GRASPrune (different post-prune accuracy profile) to break correlation | exp-005 |\n53\t\n54\t## Key Differentiations\n55\t- **vs MPruner (2024)**: inter-layer CKA for depth pruning in CNNs → RASP uses intra-layer CKA between individual heads for width pruning in reasoning LLMs, optimizing for post-recovery (not immediate) performance\n56\t- **vs Self-Healing (2025)**: tests RLVR recovery with standard pruning → RASP optimizes the pruning decision FOR recovery\n57\t- **vs RESP (Dec 2025)**: reasoning-trace calibration without recovery → RASP includes recovery-awareness in the pruning score\n58\t- **vs GRASPrune (ACL 2026)**: SOTA budgeted pruning without recovery study → GRASPrune is our primary baseline\n59\t- **vs PASER (2025)**: optimizes recovery DATA → RASP optimizes pruning STRUCTURE (complementary)\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b567d72f-e483-48d7-8fff-91c8c788b5c9","uuid":"6781b240-57a5-43cb-afe3-4d785c688a7d","timestamp":"2026-05-15T14:37:20.760Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T140651/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — recovery_aware_struct_prune\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25 submission)\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026\n\n## Core Insight (Redundancy Paradox)\nTraditional structured pruning selects structures to remove based on importance metrics alone (weight magnitude, gradient sensitivity). We show this misses a critical signal for RLVR recovery: **functional uniqueness**. Structures with high functional overlap (high CKA) can be safely pruned because RLVR redistributes their function across retained structures. Structures with low overlap are functionally irreplaceable — once removed, even RLVR cannot recreate their unique contribution. This creates a **Redundancy Paradox**: protecting functionally unique structures matters more for recovery than protecting high-importance structures.\n\nRASP exploits this via S(h) = I(h) × (1-F(h))^α: high overlap → low score → **pruned first**; low overlap → high score → **protected**. The result: RASP preferentially removes functionally redundant structures (whose function RLVR can recover) while Standard pruning may accidentally remove functionally unique structures that happen to have low importance scores. At 20% sparsity, this effect manifests entirely within MLP channel groups (0/112 attention GQA groups are pruned under either method; all 200 pruned structures are MLP groups), consistent with the \"RL Squeezes, SFT Expands\" mechanism (ICLR 2026).\n\n## Core Claims (3)\n\n1. **CKA-aware pruning preserves reasoning ability**: At matched sparsity and parameter count, RASP preserves significantly more post-prune reasoning accuracy than importance-only pruning (MVP evidence: 29% vs 1% GSM8K at 20% sparsity, p<0.0001), and this gap enables qualitatively different recovery outcomes (RASP-pruned models can be recovered via RLVR; standard-pruned models cannot).\n\n2. **Functional overlap predicts per-structure recoverability** *(scope: MLP channel groups at moderate sparsity)*: Per-structure CKA functional overlap F(h) is a stronger predictor of post-recovery accuracy retention than standard importance metrics alone, within the MLP channel groups that are actually pruned at 20-25% sparsity. At these sparsity levels, attention GQA groups consistently rank above all MLP groups in the global importance list (0/112 pruned); the CKA signal's practical effect is selecting *which* MLP groups to prune (N=784, ~200 pruned). Validated via mixed-effects regression (layer as random effect) on MLP groups, controlling for weight norm, gradient importance, and activation magnitude. Cross-component (attention + MLP) validation requires higher sparsity (~40%+).\n\n3. **Recovery method conditions optimal pruning order**: The relative ranking of pruning strategies changes depending on recovery method (RLVR vs SFT). Structures expendable under RLVR recovery may be critical under SFT recovery, consistent with the \"RL Squeezes, SFT Expands\" mechanism — RLVR compresses incorrect paths (tolerates removal of overlapping structures) while SFT expands correct paths (needs preserved trajectory-encoding structures).\n\n## Story Spine\n\n- **Problem**: Structured pruning for reasoning LLMs optimizes for immediate post-pruning accuracy, treating subsequent recovery as independent. At moderate sparsity (20-35%), this disconnect can be catastrophic: standard importance-based pruning collapses reasoning ability to near-zero, making recovery impossible regardless of method. The choice of what to prune determines whether recovery can succeed at all.\n\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Self-Healing (2025) shows RLVR recovers pruned reasoning models to 95%+ at 25% compression but uses standard pruning and tests only one ratio. GRASPrune (ACL 2026) provides SOTA budgeted structural pruning but doesn't study reasoning-specific recovery. RESP (Dec 2025) uses reasoning-trace calibration but has no recovery phase. No work studies how the pruning structure choice interacts with RLVR recovery quality, or whether optimal pruning differs for RLVR vs SFT recovery.\n\n- **Our framing**: We introduce Recovery-Aware Structured Pruning (RASP), reframing structural redundancy from a flaw to eliminate into a signal of RLVR recoverability. RASP scores structures by S(h) = I(h) × (1 - F(h))^α, protecting functionally unique reasoning scaffolding while allowing removal of structures whose function can be redistributed through RLVR. This connects to the Lottery Ticket Hypothesis at a new level: LTH asks \"which subnetwork trains well\" (binary); RASP asks \"which structures to remove so the remainder recovers well under a specific training paradigm\" (paradigm-conditioned trainability).\n\n- **Headline result template**: \"At 20% structured sparsity on DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B, RASP preserves 29% GSM8K accuracy (vs 1% for standard pruning), enabling RLVR recovery to X% while standard-pruned models remain unrecoverable. Per-structure CKA overlap explains Y% of variance in recovery outcomes (mixed-effects β = Z, p < 0.001).\"\n\n## Venue Fit\n- EMNLP Efficient Methods track: natural fit for structured pruning + reasoning model recovery\n- Reasoning model compression is timely (DeepSeek-R1, QwQ, etc. driving demand)\n- Empirical rigor + mechanistic analysis aligns with EMNLP's preference for thorough experimentation\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n- **\"Just another pruning metric\"**: Mitigate with Redundancy Paradox framing, LTH generalization (paradigm-conditioned trainability), and mechanistic analysis showing WHY it works\n- **\"Single model\"**: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B is the most widely-used open reasoning model; multi-sparsity + multi-method comparison compensates\n- **\"MPruner already uses CKA\"**: Different granularity (intra-layer per-head vs inter-layer), different objective (recoverability prediction vs redundancy removal), different domain (reasoning LLM vs CNN/general transformer)\n- **\"Cross-component pruning not observed\"**: At 20-25% sparsity, only MLP groups are pruned (0 attention groups). Framework scores both types jointly, but global ranking at moderate sparsity naturally prioritizes MLP removal. Mitigate by: (1) honest description of actual pruning distribution, (2) noting the CKA signal still drives 29% vs 1% gap via MLP group reranking, (3) optionally test higher sparsity where attention groups enter pruning range\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Experimental Responses\n\n| Concern | Response | Supporting Experiment |\n|---------|----------|----------------------|\n| Incremental over importance-only pruning | 28pp post-prune gap is qualitative, not incremental; enables vs prevents recovery | exp-001, exp-002 |\n| CKA overlap might correlate with simpler metrics | Scoring ablation: CKA vs magnitude/gradient/random | exp-007 |\n| Single model generalization | Multi-sparsity (20%, 25%, 30%) + multi-method (Standard, GRASPrune, RASP) | exp-003, exp-005 |\n| RLVR vs SFT claim needs controlled comparison | Same pruned models, same data budget, different recovery method | exp-006 |\n| Statistical rigor of correlation claim | Mixed-effects regression with covariates on MLP groups (N=784, ~200 pruned) | exp-008 |\n| Only MLP groups pruned at 20% sparsity | Honest description + CKA still drives 29% vs 1% via MLP reranking + optional higher sparsity test | experiments.tex |\n| Recovery might just reflect post-prune accuracy | Include GRASPrune (different post-prune accuracy profile) to break correlation | exp-005 |\n\n## Key Differentiations\n- **vs MPruner (2024)**: inter-layer CKA for depth pruning in CNNs → RASP uses intra-layer CKA between individual heads for width pruning in reasoning LLMs, optimizing for post-recovery (not immediate) performance\n- **vs Self-Healing (2025)**: tests RLVR recovery with standard pruning → RASP optimizes the pruning decision FOR recovery\n- **vs RESP (Dec 2025)**: reasoning-trace calibration without recovery → RASP includes recovery-awareness in the pruning score\n- **vs GRASPrune (ACL 2026)**: SOTA budgeted pruning without recovery study → GRASPrune is our primary baseline\n- **vs PASER (2025)**: optimizes recovery DATA → RASP optimizes pruning STRUCTURE (complementary)\n","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":60}}}
