{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ftp9tZiGZQi2pBVxSkJJKn","type":"tool_result","content":"440\tThese results suggest a broader principle for model compression: the structures removed should be chosen not based on their current contribution, but based on whether the recovery method can redistribute their function. When recovery uses RLVR, functional redundancy is a resource, not a liability.\n441\t\n442\t%====================================================================\n443\t% References\n444\t%====================================================================\n445\t\n446\t\\begin{thebibliography}{20}\n447\t\n448\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{DeepSeek-AI}2025]{deepseek2025r1}\n449\tDeepSeek-AI. 2025.\n450\t\\newblock DeepSeek-R1: Incentivizing Reasoning Capability in LLMs via Reinforcement Learning.\n451\t\\newblock {\\em arXiv preprint arXiv:2501.12948}.\n452\t\n453\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{QwQ Team}2024]{qwq2024}\n454\tQwQ Team. 2024.\n455\t\\newblock QwQ: Reflect Deeply on the Boundaries of the Unknown.\n456\t\\newblock {\\em Technical Report}.\n457\t\n458\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Chen et al.}2025]{selfhealing2025}\n459\tChen, X., et al. 2025.\n460\t\\newblock Self-Healing: RLVR Recovery of Pruned Reasoning Models.\n461\t\\newblock {\\em arXiv preprint}.\n462\t\n463\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Wang et al.}2026]{graspprune2026}\n464\tWang, Y., et al. 2026.\n465\t\\newblock GRASPrune: Gradient-Aware Structured Pruning with Learned Gates.\n466\t\\newblock In {\\em Proceedings of ACL 2026}.\n467\t\n468\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Zhang et al.}2025]{bonsai2025}\n469\tZhang, L., et al. 2025.\n470\t\\newblock Bonsai: Gradient-Free Structured Pruning for Large Language Models.\n471\t\\newblock In {\\em Proceedings of ICML 2025}.\n472\t\n473\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Li et al.}2025]{resp2025}\n474\tLi, H., et al. 2025.\n475\t\\newblock RESP: Reasoning-Trace Calibration for Structured Pruning.\n476\t\\ne